-mode","content":"Which run mode does a new tool use?"},"4363":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-22","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-check-auto-work","content":"How do I check what an agent did on its own?"},"4364":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-23","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-drafted-by","content":"Can I see which agent wrote an email?"},"4365":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-24","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-speakers","content":"Does Oliv AI know who said what on a call?"},"4366":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-25","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-whole-calls","content":"Does the AI read whole calls or snippets?"},"4367":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-26","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-oliver-changes","content":"Will Oliver change our process on its own?"},"4368":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-27","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-learning","content":"Do agents learn from my corrections?"},"4369":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-28","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-conflicts","content":"What happens when two sources disagree?"},"4370":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-29","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#related","content":"Related"},"4371":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-30","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","content":"Oliv AI's agents read your calls, emails and CRM, then act on what they find. This page explains how you stay in control of that work. It covers where you approve changes before they land, how run modes set an agent's freedom, what each run record shows, and how every CRM update points back to the moment in a conversation that caused it."},"4372":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-31","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#at-a-glance","content":"| Control                          | Where you set or see it    | What it guards                        |\n| -------------------------------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| **Ask First** and **Auto-Pilot** | CRM Manager's control mode | Whether CRM updates wait for a person |","table":"table-0"},"4373":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-32","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#at-a-glance","content":"| Control                                                | Where you set or see it               | What it guards                     |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| **Auto Run**, **Requires Approval**, **Agent Decides** | Each tool on an agent's **Tools** tab | Whether one action runs on its own |","table":"table-0"},"4374":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-33","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#at-a-glance","content":"| Control                                          | Where you set or see it                       | What it guards                                    |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Ask before acting** and **Act without asking** | Beneath the message box with Olivia or Oliver | How freely a super agent acts in one conversation |","table":"table-0"},"4375":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-34","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#at-a-glance","content":"| Control     | Where you set or see it | What it guards                                   |\n| ----------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| Run history | An agent's **Runs** tab | Every time the agent worked, and what it changed |","table":"table-0"},"4376":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-35","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#at-a-glance","content":"| Control             | Where you set or see it                 | What it guards                               |\n| ------------------- | --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| **Reasoning Trace** | Above each answer from Olivia or Oliver | The steps the agent took to reach the answer |","table":"table-0"},"4377":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-36","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#at-a-glance","content":"| Control       | Where you set or see it  | What it guards                                    |\n| ------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| Source moment | Each proposed CRM update | The part of the conversation the update came from |","table":"table-0"},"4378":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-37","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#review-before-change","content":"Most agent output that changes a system of record goes through a person first. You decide when that review can stop."},"4379":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-38","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#crm-updates","content":"Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent has two control modes. **Ask First** means you review each update before it's written. **Auto-Pilot** means unreviewed updates apply automatically, so the pipeline stays current without anyone acting. By default, every suggested update surfaces for review before anything reaches your CRM."},"4380":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-39","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#crm-updates","content":"On a deal's **CRM Updates** tab, **AI Suggestions** shows each proposed value beside its **Current Value**, with **Accept** and **Reject**. **AI Updates** lists changes already applied, and **Updates History** keeps the record. Once accuracy thresholds are met, RevOps confirms the switch to auto mode."},"4381":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-40","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#crm-updates","content":"Each suggested field change waits on the deal until someone accepts or rejects it, with the current CRM value shown beside it for comparison."},"4382":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-41","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#crm-updates","content":"The workflow for keeping the CRM updated walks through that review step by step, and the CRM Manager agent page covers the agent itself."},"4383":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-42","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#crm-updates","content":"Oliv AI's Meeting Assistant agent works the same way after a call. It reads the call, finds what changed, and proposes updates for approval. The Meeting Assistant agent then hands approved changes to CRM Manager to write."},"4384":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-43","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#crm-updates","content":"A meeting's own **CRM Updates** tab lists what was written after the call, such as a refreshed account summary or a new contact. A bigger change, such as a stage move, waits as **Pending Update** until you press **Update Deal**."},"4385":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-44","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#crm-updates","content":"After a call, completed CRM writes and changes still waiting for you sit in one timeline, so you can see what landed and what needs a decision."},"4386":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-45","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#process-changes","content":"Oliv AI's Oliver agent keeps your process handbook: ICP, personas, methodology and approval rules. It surfaces patterns and drafts recommendations as proposals marked **Pending Review**."},"4387":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-46","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#process-changes","content":"**Review changes** shows each affected file as a line-by-line diff, then lists the knock-on effects. You choose **Approve & merge**, **Request edit** or **Cancel**, and an approved change shows as **Merged**. A minor update, such as syncing an agent prompt to a scorecard, can apply as **Autonomous**. The **History** tab logs it as \"No human review needed\". More on how that works is on the Oliver agent page."},"4388":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-47","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#process-changes","content":"Every playbook change carries a status, so you can tell what Oliv AI's Oliver agent is waiting on and what it applied without a review."},"4389":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-48","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#coaching-and-forecasts","content":"Oliv AI's Coach agent drafts monthly recommendations for each rep, each with evidence attached. A manager can accept a recommendation as written, edit it or override it. Nothing reaches the rep until the manager has reviewed it. The Coach agent page has the full cycle."},"4390":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-49","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#coaching-and-forecasts","content":"Oliv AI's Forecaster agent shows its signals for rep or manager review. Reps and managers can accept, edit or reject each one, and that feedback trains the agent. The Forecaster agent explains how signals roll up into the forecast."},"4391":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-50","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-modes","content":"A tool is one action an agent is allowed to take, such as updating a CRM record or sending an email. Every tool an agent holds carries one of three settings:"},"4392":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-51","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-modes","content":"| Run mode     | What it does                 |\n| ------------ | ---------------------------- |\n| **Auto Run** | The tool acts without asking |","table":"table-1"},"4393":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-52","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-modes","content":"| Run mode              | What it does                           |\n| --------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| **Requires Approval** | The tool needs a person's confirmation |","table":"table-1"},"4394":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-53","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-modes","content":"| Run mode          | What it does                    |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| **Agent Decides** | The agent judges whether to ask |","table":"table-1"},"4395":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-54","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-modes","content":"The mode is set per tool, on each agent, so changing one tool changes nothing else. Auto Run is the default for any tool that doesn't state another mode. That matters most for tools that write: Auto Run on a CRM, mailbox or channel tool means the agent may write to that system without asking."},"4396":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-55","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-modes","content":"Check each tool before you switch an agent on."},"4397":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-56","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-modes","content":"The run mode sits on each tool card, so you can see at a glance which actions an agent will take without asking."},"4398":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-57","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-modes","content":"The tools and run modes guide shows where the control sits. The agent builder overview explains how tools fit alongside an agent's instructions and the triggers that start it."},"4399":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-58","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#super-agent-setting","content":"Oliv AI's Olivia agent and Oliv AI's Oliver agent carry a second, separate control. It sets how freely the super agent acts for a whole conversation: **Ask before acting** or **Act without asking**. It sits beneath the message box and opens on **Ask before acting**."},"4400":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-59","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#super-agent-setting","content":"With Olivia on **Ask before acting**, she aligns on her approach before taking actions. Setting Oliver to **Act without asking** shows a **High Risk** warning above the message box, because Oliver can then change your settings. The Olivia agent page covers working with her day to day."},"4401":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-60","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-records","content":"Run history is the record of every time an agent has worked. It's how you check that an agent on auto-pilot has been doing the right thing. The **Runs** tab holds a **Run history** table with **Time**, **Type** and **Status** columns, a **View** link on each row and a search box for previous runs. It also shows whether a run was automatic or manual, so you can see how much the agent did on its own."},"4402":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-61","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-records","content":"The Type column shows which runs a trigger started on its own, so you know which records to check first."},"4403":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-62","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-records","content":"Pressing **View** on a run opens its full record:"},"4404":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-63","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-records","content":"**The people it touched.** A **Top Identified Contacts** panel lists them."},"4405":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-64","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-records","content":"**Every email in full.** Each one sits under an **Email Sent** banner, with recipient, subject and body."},"4406":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-65","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-records","content":"**Meetings it booked.** A calendar card shows the date, time and attendees."},"4407":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-66","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-records","content":"**Changes it made elsewhere.** Under **Auto-actions logged**, each change has a timestamp and a description."},"4408":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-67","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-records","content":"**Work that needed a person.** An amber alert panel marks what the agent escalated, separate from what it did alone."},"4409":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-68","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#run-records","content":"When one agent produces work for another, the email carries a **Drafted by** line naming the agent that wrote it. That matters when Oliv AI's Olivia agent hands a task to a specialist. The run history guide explains each table and the record drawer."},"4410":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-69","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#source-moments","content":"Every CRM update comes from a conversation, and it says why. A meeting's **CRM Updates** tab lists each change that call produced, with the reason: a pending stage move to Proposal, for example, says the opportunity stage needs to be updated because the buyer asked for a formal proposal. The deal's **CRM Updates** tab shows the field, its **Current Value** and the suggested value, and **Updates History** keeps the record of how each field has been updated."},"4411":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-70","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#source-moments","content":"So when a close date moves, you can see what was said before you accept it. The same holds for the custom fields in your CRM field mapping, whether you run Salesforce or HubSpot."},"4412":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-71","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#source-moments","content":"Other agents attach evidence too:"},"4413":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-72","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#source-moments","content":"**Expansion signals.** When Oliv AI's Gold Digger agent spots one, its notification carries what was said, who said it, which account and the exact moment in the recording."},"4414":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-73","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#source-moments","content":"**Account risk.** Every flag from Oliv AI's Portfolio Manager agent comes with the evidence behind it: the signal, the account context and a recommended next action."},"4415":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-74","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#source-moments","content":"**Coaching goals.** Oliv AI's Coach agent grounds each goal in the rep's own call data and deal outcomes, so the evidence is there to discuss."},"4416":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-75","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#speaker-attribution","content":"The Converse app transcribes and labels every speaker on a recorded call. Oliv AI's context graph then connects each conversation, message and activity to the right people, account and opportunity. Your agents know who said what, and which deal it belongs to."},"4417":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-76","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#speaker-attribution","content":"That attribution is what lets a meeting summary or a proposed field update name the buyer behind a statement. For how transcription tools differ on accuracy, Oliv AI's guide to meeting transcription software compares the field."},"4418":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-77","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#what-the-ai-reads","content":"Oliv AI's answers draw on your own conversations, records and playbook. Three design choices shape how it reads them:"},"4419":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-78","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#what-the-ai-reads","content":"**Whole conversations, not fragments.** Every meeting, email and note is read end to end, with no chunking. Signals are precomputed per deal, per account and per contact."},"4420":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-79","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#what-the-ai-reads","content":"**Your playbook first.** Every agent reads the process graph before it acts. An agent working from it understands gaps and proceeds with caution, looping in a person instead of acting on outdated knowledge."},"4421":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-80","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#what-the-ai-reads","content":"**Conflicts shown, not hidden.** When two of your sources disagree, the process graph documents the conflict. It also knows when a question needs routing to a person rather than an answer."},"4422":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-81","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#reasoning-trace","content":"Every answer from Olivia or Oliver carries a **Reasoning Trace** row. It stays collapsed until you open it. For a question about stalled deals, Oliver's trace lists **Flagging stalled deals**, **Detecting filters based on query**, **Aggregating deal signals** and **Ranking by impact**, then **Done**."},"4423":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-82","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#reasoning-trace","content":"Each step says what it did, such as the filters it built from your question. The signals step names the sources it read: meetings, CRM notes, emails and account news. You can check that logic before you act on the answer."},"4424":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-83","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#reasoning-trace","content":"Open the trace to see the filters and sources behind an answer from Oliv AI's Oliver agent before you rely on it. The pipeline figures are sample values."},"4425":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-84","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#reasoning-trace","content":"For why this matters to RevOps, Oliv AI's post on autonomous CRM hygiene sets out the data-quality case."},"4426":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-85","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#feedback","content":"Your reviews do more than gate one change. Oliv AI's Forecaster agent learns from every signal you accept, edit or reject. Oliv AI's Portfolio Manager agent learns when you dismiss a flag that doesn't match your read. Oliv AI's Oliver agent watches what is winning in the field and drafts the next process update for your review."},"4427":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-86","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#review-first-rollout","content":"This pattern keeps every write visible until your team trusts the agents:"},"4428":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-87","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#review-first-rollout","content":"**Start CRM updates on Ask First.** Reps accept or reject each suggestion for the first weeks."},"4429":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-88","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#review-first-rollout","content":"**Set write tools to Requires Approval.** Leave read-only lookups on Auto Run."},"4430":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-89","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#review-first-rollout","content":"**Read run history weekly.** Open a few records and check the emails and logged changes."},"4431":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-90","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#review-first-rollout","content":"**Watch acceptance by rep.** Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent sends a weekly governance summary with acceptance rate by rep and flags requiring review."},"4432":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-91","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#review-first-rollout","content":"**Switch to auto per area.** When accuracy thresholds are met, RevOps confirms the move to Auto-Pilot."},"4433":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-92","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#review-first-rollout","content":"The record and follow up workflow shows the post-call review in practice, and Slack notifications tell reps when updates are waiting."},"4434":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-93","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#limits","content":"**Two controls, two places.** Tool run modes are set per tool on each agent. The conversation setting is set per conversation with Olivia or Oliver. Changing one leaves the other as it was."},"4435":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-94","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#limits","content":"**Auto Run is the starting point.** A tool with no stated mode runs as Auto Run, so review write tools before an agent goes live."},"4436":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-95","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#limits","content":"**Auto modes skip review.** On **Auto-Pilot** or **Auto Run**, changes land without a person in the loop. Run history is where you check them afterward."},"4437":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-96","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#limits","content":"**Run records are read-only.** A record shows what a run did. Approval happens in the review step, not in the record."},"4438":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-97","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#limits","content":"**Minor playbook updates can skip review.** **History** marks them **Autonomous**, so read it alongside run history."},"4439":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-98","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#limits","content":"**Oliver's warning is specific.** The **High Risk** warning appears for Oliver on **Act without asking**, because Oliver can change settings."},"4440":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-99","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-crm-approval","content":"Only if you allow it. By default, every suggested update surfaces for review before anything reaches your CRM. RevOps confirms the switch to auto mode once accuracy thresholds are met."},"4441":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-100","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-why-change","content":"Each proposed update includes its source, the exact moment in the conversation that triggered it. The **CRM Updates** tab shows the field, its current value and the suggested value."},"4442":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-101","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-reasoning-trace","content":"Yes. Open the **Reasoning Trace** row above an answer from Olivia or Oliver. It lists each step, the filters it applied and the sources it read."},"4443":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-102","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-two-controls","content":"**Requires Approval** is a run mode on one tool of one agent. **Ask before acting** is a setting for a whole conversation with Olivia or Oliver. They're separate controls."},"4444":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-103","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-default-mode","content":"Auto Run, unless the tool states another mode. Set write tools to **Requires Approval** if you want a person to confirm each action."},"4445":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-104","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-check-auto-work","content":"Open the agent's **Runs** tab. It shows whether each run was automatic or manual, and **View** opens the full record, including logged changes with timestamps."},"4446":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-105","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-drafted-by","content":"Yes. When one agent produces work for another, the email carries a **Drafted by** line naming the agent that wrote it."},"4447":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-106","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-speakers","content":"Yes. Converse transcribes and labels every speaker, and the context graph ties each conversation to the right people, account and opportunity."},"4448":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-107","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-whole-calls","content":"Whole calls. Every meeting, email and note is read end to end, with no chunking, and signals are precomputed per deal, account and contact."},"4449":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-108","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-oliver-changes","content":"Process proposals wait as **Pending Review** until someone presses **Approve & merge**, then show as **Merged**. Minor updates can apply as **Autonomous**, and **History** logs each one."},"4450":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-109","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-learning","content":"Some do. Forecaster learns from the signals you accept, edit or reject. Portfolio Manager learns from the flags you dismiss."},"4451":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-110","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#faq-conflicts","content":"The process graph documents the conflict instead of hiding it. An agent facing a gap loops in a person rather than acting on outdated knowledge."},"4452":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-111","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#related","content":"Agent tools and run modes: set each tool's freedom to act."},"4453":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-112","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#related","content":"Agent run history: read every run and what it changed."},"4454":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-113","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#related","content":"Keep the CRM updated: the review-then-auto path for CRM writes."},"4455":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-114","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#related","content":"Oliver agent: process changes that wait for your approval."},"4456":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-115","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#related","content":"CRM Manager agent: the agent that writes approved updates."},"4457":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-116","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#related","content":"Deal Driver agent: risk alerts grounded in your qualification framework."},"4458":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-117","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#related","content":"Agents overview: every documented agent."},"4459":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy-118","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/ai-quality-and-accuracy#related","content":"Oliv AI product documentation: every documented agent and feature."},"4460":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"page","content":"Context, process and signal graphs","breadcrumbs":["Oliv AI docs","Platform"],"tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs"},"4461":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-0","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","content":"The three graphs underneath Oliv AI's agents, what each one holds, how it stays current, and which agents read it before they act."},"4462":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-1","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance"},"4463":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-2","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#data-sources","content":"Where the graphs get their data"},"4464":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-3","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#context-graph","content":"Context graph"},"4465":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-4","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#how-mapping-works","content":"How an activity finds its place"},"4466":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-5","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#mapping-cases","content":"The cases it's built for"},"4467":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-6","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#context-graph-readers","content":"Who reads it"},"4468":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-7","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#context-graph-in-product","content":"Where you see it"},"4469":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-8","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph","content":"Process graph"},"4470":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-9","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-layers","content":"Three layers"},"4471":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-10","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-upkeep","content":"How it's built and kept current"},"4472":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-11","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-in-product","content":"Where you see it"},"4473":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-12","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-readers","content":"Who reads it"},"4474":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-13","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-graph","content":"Signal graph"},"4475":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-14","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#why-precompute","content":"Why precompute"},"4476":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-15","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-models","content":"What the models cover"},"4477":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-16","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-tuning","content":"Tuned to what you sell"},"4478":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-17","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-graph-readers","content":"Who reads it"},"4479":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-18","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-graph-in-product","content":"Where you see it"},"4480":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-19","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#limits","content":"Limits and things to know"},"4481":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-20","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#common-questions","content":"Common questions"},"4482":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-21","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-difference","content":"What is the difference between the three graphs?"},"4483":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-22","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-clean-crm","content":"Do I need a clean CRM before the context graph works?"},"4484":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-23","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-multi-account-call","content":"What happens when one call covers several customer accounts?"},"4485":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-24","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-acquisition","content":"What if a customer is acquired and emails from a new domain?"},"4486":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-25","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-content","content":"Does Oliv AI keep the content of calls and emails, or only metadata?"},"4487":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-26","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-process-readers","content":"Which agents read the process graph?"},"4488":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-27","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-playbook-change","content":"How does a playbook change reach every agent?"},"4489":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-28","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-documents","content":"Can the process graph learn from our existing documents?"},"4490":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-29","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-personal-memory","content":"Is personal memory shared with my manager?"},"4491":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-30","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-model-count","content":"How many signal models are there?"},"4492":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-31","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-tuning","content":"Are the signals tuned to what we sell?"},"4493":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-32","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-warehouse","content":"Does Oliv AI pull in product usage and billing data?"},"4494":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-33","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#related","content":"Related"},"4495":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-34","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","content":"Oliv AI's agents don't start from a blank page each time you ask them something. Three graphs sit underneath them. The context graph places every activity on the right account and opportunity. The process graph holds how your company sells. The signal graph stores precomputed answers to the revenue questions teams ask most. This page explains what each one holds and which agents read it."},"4496":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-35","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#at-a-glance","content":"| Graph             | What it holds                                                                                 | Who reads it                                 | How it stays current                      | Where you see it                                                                        |\n| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Context graph** | Every conversation, message and activity, mapped to the right people, account and opportunity | Every agent that needs to know who said what | Each new activity is mapped as it arrives | An account's **Timeline** and **Contacts** tabs, and a contact's **Associated Objects** |","table":"table-0"},"4497":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-36","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#at-a-glance","content":"| Graph             | What it holds                                               | Who reads it                        | How it stays current                                                            | Where you see it                           |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Process graph** | Your playbook: ICP, approval flows, methodology, exceptions | Every Oliv AI agent, before it acts | Oliver proposes changes for approval, and every change is logged in **History** | **Playbook**, at the bottom of the sidebar |","table":"table-0"},"4498":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-37","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#at-a-glance","content":"| Graph            | What it holds                                                                      | Who reads it                    | How it stays current               | Where you see it                            |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| **Signal graph** | Precomputed answers from 100+ small language models, per deal, account and contact | The AI answering your questions | Updated as new information arrives | A deal's **Health** tab, among other places |","table":"table-0"},"4499":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-38","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#at-a-glance","content":"Oliv AI is a layer that sits on top of your existing CRM rather than replacing it. The graphs add context to what your CRM already holds."},"4500":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-39","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#data-sources","content":"Every signal flows into one foundation first: calls, emails, meetings, CRM fields, docs and product usage. From there it's enriched and ready to reason over."},"4501":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-40","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#data-sources","content":"Conversations are the starting point, not the whole picture:"},"4502":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-41","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#data-sources","content":"**Your data warehouse.** Product usage, support tickets, billing history and onboarding completion. Oliv AI connects to Snowflake, Databricks, Redshift and BigQuery."},"4503":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-42","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#data-sources","content":"**Shared channels with customers.** Decisions often get made in channels shared between companies. Oliv AI monitors them and makes that context available to your AI."},"4504":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-43","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#data-sources","content":"**Your connected tools.** The integrations overview lists what connects, including Slack and the Converse app for meetings and calls."},"4505":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-44","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#data-sources","content":"An account's **Timeline**, under **Records › Companies**, shows that mix in one feed. Its filters cover **Communication** (**Calls**, **Conversations**, **Email**, **LinkedIn**, **SMS**, **WhatsApp**) and **Contact Activity**, such as **Ads Activity**, **Form submissions** and **Marketing events**. News about the account appears there too."},"4506":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-45","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#data-sources","content":"One account, every source: calls, email, marketing touches and news land on the same timeline, which is the raw material the three graphs are built from."},"4507":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-46","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#data-sources","content":"Each activity keeps its full content. An email, call, calendar event or Slack message is captured as a rich context object with participants, content and timestamps, not just its metadata."},"4508":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-47","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#context-graph","content":"The context graph connects every conversation, message and activity to the right people, account and opportunity. Your agents know who said what, and which account or opportunity it belongs to. Over time it becomes the full story of every account, built as a memory."},"4509":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-48","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#how-mapping-works","content":"A simple lookup matches the email domain and takes the first account. That breaks on a messy CRM. The context graph works through four steps instead:"},"4510":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-49","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#how-mapping-works","content":"**Capture the full activity.** Participants, content and timestamps, not only the metadata."},"4511":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-50","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#how-mapping-works","content":"**Pull every candidate object.** All accounts, opportunities and contacts, including acquisition links found through live web research."},"4512":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-51","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#how-mapping-works","content":"**Reason through the full picture.** Recency, engagement history, conversation content and relationship context decide the mapping."},"4513":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-52","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#how-mapping-works","content":"**Clean the CRM along the way.** Activity lands in the right place, and duplicates get cleaned up as a byproduct."},"4514":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-53","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#mapping-cases","content":"| Situation                             | What goes wrong with a lookup                          | What the context graph weighs                            |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Two open opportunities in one account | Activity is filed against one and the other is ignored | Which buying group and product the conversation is about |","table":"table-1"},"4515":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-54","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#mapping-cases","content":"| Situation                                         | What goes wrong with a lookup               | What the context graph weighs               |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| One partner call covering three customer accounts | Everything is logged to the partner account | Each customer account and its opportunities |","table":"table-1"},"4516":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-55","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#mapping-cases","content":"| Situation                                           | What goes wrong with a lookup                                 | What the context graph weighs                   |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| A customer acquired, now emailing from a new domain | The unknown domain finds no match and the activity is dropped | Acquisition links surfaced through web research |","table":"table-1"},"4517":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-56","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#mapping-cases","content":"| Situation                         | What goes wrong with a lookup  | What the context graph weighs                          |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| The same account in the CRM twice | One record is picked at random | Recency and engagement signals to find the live record |","table":"table-1"},"4518":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-57","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#context-graph-readers","content":"Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent maps every activity to the right account and opportunity the way a seller would. If it can't resolve a match, it asks the seller. Oliv AI's Gold Digger agent uses the context graph to understand what a customer already uses before it flags an expansion signal. The CRM Manager agent page covers how mapped activity reaches Salesforce and HubSpot."},"4519":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-58","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#context-graph-in-product","content":"The mapping shows up wherever a record lists the people and activity tied to it. An account's **Contacts** tab groups people into **Buying Committee** and **Other Contacts**, each with a sentiment face. Select a person to see role tags such as **Economic Buyer**, plus their **Pain and Needs** and **Objections**, drawn from calls and emails. A contact's **Associated Objects** tab works the other way round: it lists every deal and company the person is tied to, with their role on each deal, such as **Champion** or **Technical Evaluator**."},"4520":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-59","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#context-graph-in-product","content":"The context graph at work on one account: each person is placed on the buying committee with a role and a sentiment, and their pains and objections come from the conversations mapped to them."},"4521":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-60","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#context-graph-in-product","content":"More on the mapping is on Oliv AI's context graph page, and its post on enriching your CRM without replacing it explains the sync."},"4522":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-61","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph","content":"The process graph is the living playbook every Oliv AI agent reads before it acts. It documents your processes, judgment calls and company knowledge in a form agents can reason from, not just retrieve. It's a set of linked documents: proposal connects to approval, which links to discount authority and back to your ICP. It records how your company does operate, not how it should."},"4523":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-62","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-layers","content":"| Layer               | What it holds                                                       | Who sees it                           |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| **Global Handbook** | Company ICP, approval flows, pricing logic, competitive positioning | Shared across every agent in your org |","table":"table-2"},"4524":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-63","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-layers","content":"| Layer             | What it holds                                                                                           | Who sees it |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Agent Context** | What each specialist agent needs, such as the qualifying criteria Oliv AI's Prospector agent works from | That agent  |","table":"table-2"},"4525":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-64","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-layers","content":"| Layer               | What it holds                                           | Who sees it                                        |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Personal Memory** | A rep's current accounts, focus areas and working style | Private to that rep, maintained by their own agent |","table":"table-2"},"4526":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-65","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-upkeep","content":"Oliv AI learns your product, qualification criteria, processes and exceptions from your documentation and from what happens in the field. You bring the knowledge, and there's no cleanup sprint or CRM audit first."},"4527":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-66","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-upkeep","content":"Oliv AI's Oliver agent keeps the playbook current. When RevOps changes the ICP, every agent reflects that change: one update, consistent across the revenue org. Oliver also watches what's winning in the field and drafts the next process update for your review."},"4528":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-67","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-upkeep","content":"Oliver's proposals wait as **Pending Review** until your company approves them. You read a line-by-line diff of each affected file, then choose **Approve & merge**, **Request edit** or **Cancel**. Small changes, such as an agent prompt synced to a scorecard, apply as **Autonomous**, with no human review needed. The Oliver agent page shows how a proposed change is reviewed."},"4529":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-68","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-upkeep","content":"Every change to the process graph is logged with its author and status, so you can see what is waiting for approval, what was merged and what Oliver applied on its own."},"4530":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-69","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-in-product","content":"The process graph lives in **Playbook**, pinned at the bottom of the sidebar. It's a tree of markdown files in folders such as **Market**, **Prospecting** and **Sales**, each with **Edit** and **History** tabs and a **Synced** status. Files link to each other: **Sales Process.md**, for example, links to the selling-scenario and discovery files it builds on. Oliver's panel sits on the right, so you can ask for a change in plain language."},"4531":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-70","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-in-product","content":"The process graph as you edit it: linked playbook files that every agent reads, with Oliver beside them proposing the next change."},"4532":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-71","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-in-product","content":"When two sources disagree, the process graph documents the conflict instead of hiding it. An agent working from it understands gaps and loops in a person instead of acting on outdated knowledge."},"4533":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-72","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-readers","content":"Every agent. Some of what each one takes from it:"},"4534":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-73","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-readers","content":"**Oliv AI's Olivia agent** operates inside the stages, ownership and handoffs Oliver sets, from day one. See the Olivia agent."},"4535":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-74","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-readers","content":"**Oliv AI's Coach agent** coaches every rep against the same up-to-date methodology. See the Coach agent."},"4536":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-75","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-readers","content":"**Oliv AI's Deal Driver agent** grounds its alerts in your qualification framework. See the Deal Driver agent."},"4537":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-76","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-readers","content":"**Oliv AI's Forecaster agent** builds its signals on that framework, so the forecast rests on one qualification standard. See the Forecaster agent."},"4538":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-77","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-readers","content":"**Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent** tracks and updates the fields Oliver defines, including those in your CRM field mapping."},"4539":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-78","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#process-graph-readers","content":"For agents you build yourself, agent instructions and knowledge files add focused context on top. Oliv AI's process graph page has more on the layers."},"4540":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-79","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-graph","content":"The signal graph stores the answers to common revenue questions before anyone asks them. Oliv AI runs 100+ specialized small language models, each fine-tuned to answer one revenue question. They read every meeting, email and note end to end, with no chunking. The answers are precomputed per deal, per account and per contact, and updated as new information arrives."},"4541":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-80","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#why-precompute","content":"Revenue teams ask many of the same questions about every account. What are the pains? Who decides? What's the budget? Retrieving a few similar-looking fragments at question time loses the thread across meetings. The signal graph reads the full history instead, so the model receiving your question gets complete context, not fragments. Oliv AI reads context, sentiment and intent rather than matching keywords."},"4542":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-81","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-models","content":"The models span the revenue lifecycle, before and after the sale. A sample:"},"4543":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-82","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-models","content":"| Stage         | Example signals                                                                                  |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Qualification | Pains and needs, budget availability, decision criteria, economic buyer, champion identification |","table":"table-3"},"4544":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-83","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-models","content":"| Stage         | Example signals                                                               |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Deal progress | Next steps, risk signals, buying committee, objection tracking, deal velocity |","table":"table-3"},"4545":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-84","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-models","content":"| Stage       | Example signals                                          |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Methodology | MEDDIC scoring, MEDDPICC score, BANT score, SPICED score |","table":"table-3"},"4546":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-85","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-models","content":"| Stage     | Example signals                                                                                       |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Post-sale | Renewal risk score, expansion signals, executive sponsor health, product adoption gaps, QBR readiness |","table":"table-3"},"4547":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-86","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-tuning","content":"Each model is further tuned to your business, because the pains a developer tools vendor hears differ from those a RevOps platform hears. Tuning runs on a short schedule:"},"4548":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-87","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-tuning","content":"**Day 0, at proof of value kickoff.** Oliv AI's agent studies your website, product pages and positioning."},"4549":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-88","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-tuning","content":"**Day 1.** Each model gets a tailored prompt that limits it to signals relevant to your solution."},"4550":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-89","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-tuning","content":"**Week 1 onward.** Human feedback and quarterly re-research track new offerings, positioning and buyer personas."},"4551":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-90","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-graph-readers","content":"The AI answering your question uses those precomputed answers instead of rebuilding context from raw history. Ask which deals are likely to close this quarter, and the answer comes from checking each deal's pain point, compelling event, timeline and MEDDPICC signals. That's the kind of question you'd bring to a pipeline review or to meeting prep."},"4552":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-91","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-graph-in-product","content":"Per-deal answers surface on each deal in **Records › Deals**. The **Health** tab has sub-tabs for **Forecast**, **Risks**, **Qualification**, **Competition**, **Objections**, **Buying Committee** and **POC Health**. The **Forecast** sub-tab reads out a win probability, how many MEDDPICC criteria are confirmed, how often the close date has slipped, and the one thing dragging the score down. On an account, the **Point of View** tab lists intent signals such as **Expansion Momentum** and **Leadership / Org Change**."},"4553":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-92","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-graph-in-product","content":"Signals read out per deal: the Health tab answers whether the deal will close, what is putting it at risk and what to do next, without anyone rebuilding the history first."},"4554":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-93","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#signal-graph-in-product","content":"Oliv AI's signal graph page shows the model library. Its posts on meaning extraction versus raw transcripts and why retrieval fails on CRM data go deeper on the reasoning."},"4555":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-94","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#limits","content":"**Your CRM stays the system of record.** Oliv AI works on top of it and enriches it; it doesn't replace it."},"4556":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-95","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#limits","content":"**Unclear matches go to a person.** When Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent can't resolve where an activity belongs, it asks the seller."},"4557":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-96","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#limits","content":"**Process changes are reviewed or logged.** Oliver's larger proposals wait as **Pending Review** for a person to approve. Minor changes can apply as **Autonomous**, and every change appears in the Playbook's **History**."},"4558":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-97","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#limits","content":"**Personal memory stays personal.** It's visible only to the rep it belongs to."},"4559":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-98","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#limits","content":"**Signal models start general, then get tuned.** They run out of the box and are tuned to your business from the proof of value kickoff."},"4560":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-99","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-difference","content":"The context graph places each activity on the right account and opportunity. The process graph holds how your company sells. The signal graph stores precomputed answers to revenue questions, per deal, account and contact."},"4561":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-100","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-clean-crm","content":"No. It's built for messy data: duplicate records, several open opportunities and changed email domains. It cleans duplicates as a byproduct of mapping."},"4562":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-101","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-multi-account-call","content":"The context graph weighs each customer account and its opportunities, instead of logging everything to the partner who joined the call."},"4563":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-102","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-acquisition","content":"The context graph pulls acquisition links found through live web research, so the activity can still reach the open opportunity."},"4564":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-103","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-content","content":"The content. Each activity is captured as a rich context object with participants, content and timestamps."},"4565":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-104","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-process-readers","content":"Every Oliv AI agent reads it before it acts. Olivia, Coach, Deal Driver, Forecaster and CRM Manager each draw on it."},"4566":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-105","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-playbook-change","content":"You tell Oliver what changed, or edit the file in **Playbook** yourself. When RevOps changes the ICP, every agent reflects it once the change is merged. Oliver's own proposals wait as **Pending Review** until someone approves them."},"4567":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-106","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-documents","content":"Yes. Oliv AI learns your product, qualification criteria, processes and exceptions from your documentation and from what happens in the field."},"4568":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-107","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-personal-memory","content":"No. Personal memory is private to each rep, maintained by their own agent and visible only to them."},"4569":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-108","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-model-count","content":"More than 100 out of the box, each fine-tuned to answer one revenue question, across pre-sales and post-sales."},"4570":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-109","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-tuning","content":"Yes. Each model gets a tailored prompt from the first day of your proof of value. Human feedback and quarterly re-research keep it current as your offering changes."},"4571":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-110","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#faq-warehouse","content":"Yes. It connects to Snowflake, Databricks, Redshift and BigQuery for product usage, support tickets, billing history and onboarding completion."},"4572":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-111","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#related","content":"Oliver agent: the agent that keeps the process graph current."},"4573":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-112","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#related","content":"CRM Manager agent: mapped activity written back to your CRM."},"4574":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-113","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#related","content":"Keep the CRM updated: the workflow built on the context graph."},"4575":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-114","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#related","content":"Run deals as an account executive: the graphs at work across a rep's week."},"4576":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-115","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#related","content":"Agents overview: every documented agent."},"4577":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs-116","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/graphs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/graphs#related","content":"Oliv AI product documentation: every documented agent and feature."},"4578":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm","type":"page","content":"Oliv AI and your CRM","breadcrumbs":["Oliv AI docs","Platform"],"tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm"},"4579":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm-0","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm","content":"How Oliv AI works as a layer on top of Salesforce, HubSpot or Zoho, what it reads and writes back, how updates are approved, and why your CRM stays the system of record."},"4580":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm-1","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance"},"4581":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm-2","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm#what-it-is","content":"How Oliv AI sits on your CRM"},"4582":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm-3","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm#one-product","content":"One product across the revenue team"},"4583":{"id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm-4","page_id":"/product-docs/platform/oliv-and-your-crm","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/platform/ol