ags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#customer-success","content":"Customer success and account management"},"5063":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-27","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare","content":"How keeping the CRM updated compares"},"5064":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-28","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare-stronger","content":"Why Oliv AI is the stronger choice for keeping the CRM updated"},"5065":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-29","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#limits","content":"Limits and things to know"},"5066":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-30","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#common-questions","content":"Common questions"},"5067":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-31","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-clean-crm","content":"Do I need a clean CRM before I start?"},"5068":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-32","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-direct-write","content":"Does CRM Manager write directly to my CRM?"},"5069":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-33","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-wrong-update","content":"What if it makes a wrong update?"},"5070":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-34","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-crms","content":"Which CRMs are supported?"},"5071":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-35","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-custom-fields","content":"Who sets up custom fields?"},"5072":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-36","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-hierarchy","content":"Does it understand account hierarchies?"},"5073":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-37","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-customer-success","content":"Does it work for customer success as well as sales?"},"5074":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-38","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-weekly-report","content":"What does RevOps get each week?"},"5075":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-39","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-pending","content":"Can managers see what's waiting for review?"},"5076":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-40","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-field-history","content":"Can I see how a field changed over time?"},"5077":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-41","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"Related"},"5078":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-42","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","content":"Oliv AI keeps your CRM current from the work your team already does. Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent reads every meeting, call and email, then updates accounts, contacts, opportunities, activities and tasks in Salesforce, HubSpot or Zoho. You review each proposed change before it's written, then switch to auto mode once you trust it. This guide covers setting it up and running a monthly hygiene check."},"5079":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-43","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#at-a-glance","content":"|                       |                             |\n| --------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| **Who does the work** | Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent |","table":"table-0"},"5080":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-44","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#at-a-glance","content":"|          |                              |\n| -------- | ---------------------------- |\n| **CRMs** | Salesforce, HubSpot and Zoho |","table":"table-0"},"5081":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-45","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#at-a-glance","content":"|                     |                                                         |\n| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **What it updates** | Accounts, contacts, opportunities, activities and tasks |","table":"table-0"},"5082":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-46","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#at-a-glance","content":"|            |                                                            |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Fields** | Standard fields, methodology fields and your custom fields |","table":"table-0"},"5083":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-47","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#at-a-glance","content":"|                 |                               |\n| --------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| **Starts from** | Every meeting, call and email |","table":"table-0"},"5084":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-48","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#at-a-glance","content":"|             |                                                                          |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Control** | **Ask First** to review each update, or **Auto-Pilot** once you trust it |","table":"table-0"},"5085":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-49","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#at-a-glance","content":"|                      |                                                       |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Where you review** | The deal's **CRM Updates** tab in **Records › Deals** |","table":"table-0"},"5086":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-50","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#at-a-glance","content":"|                |                                                    |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| **For RevOps** | A weekly report and batch clean-up jobs on request |","table":"table-0"},"5087":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-51","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#before-you-begin","content":"**Connect your CRM.** Salesforce, HubSpot and Zoho are supported out of the box. Additional CRMs are available on request."},"5088":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-52","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#before-you-begin","content":"**Plan your custom fields.** Oliv's team maps fields unique to your process during onboarding, as a service."},"5089":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-53","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#before-you-begin","content":"**Don't clean first.** CRM Manager is built to start on messy data. It cleans as it goes and can work back through old records."},"5090":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-54","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#before-you-begin","content":"**Agree who reviews.** In the review phase, reps accept or reject updates. RevOps decides when to switch to auto mode."},"5091":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-55","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-1-connect-crm","content":"Connect Salesforce, HubSpot or Zoho. Your pipeline and fields sync once the CRM is connected. Standard fields such as close date, deal amount, stage, next steps and last activity date are pre-mapped, so they populate from day one. Oliv AI works on top of your CRM, so every update flows into the workflows, reports and dashboards you already use."},"5092":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-56","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-1-connect-crm","content":"Then check your stages in **Settings › Revenue Process**. **Import Pipeline from CRM** pulls in the stages from the connected CRM, with a tab for each sales motion. Each deal's header also carries **Sync to Salesforce** to push the deal to the CRM."},"5093":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-57","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-1-connect-crm","content":"Importing your pipeline gives CRM Manager the same stages your CRM uses. Stage moves it suggests later will then match the stages and forecast categories your reports expect."},"5094":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-58","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-2-activity","content":"There's nothing to schedule. From the first meeting, call or email, Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent is already working. It's the idea behind autonomous CRM hygiene: no rules to maintain. After each activity it:"},"5095":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-59","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-2-activity","content":"Creates accounts and contacts that aren't in the CRM yet, and enriches them."},"5096":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-60","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-2-activity","content":"Logs the meeting, call or email against the right account, contact and opportunity."},"5097":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-61","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-2-activity","content":"Creates tasks from next steps, and assigns each one to the right rep or owner."},"5098":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-62","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-2-activity","content":"Updates deal stage as the deal moves, and writes methodology fields for the framework marked **Active** in **Settings › Qualification Framework**."},"5099":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-63","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-2-activity","content":"Tracks each contact's role on the deal, such as economic buyer, champion or blocker."},"5100":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-64","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-2-activity","content":"If it can't work out which account or opportunity an activity belongs to, it asks the seller."},"5101":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-65","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-2-activity","content":"Each meeting's **CRM Updates** tab, in **Activities › Meetings**, lists what was written after the call. Completed cards such as **Account Updated** and **Contact Created** link to the record. A stage move waits as **Pending Update** until you press **Update Deal**."},"5102":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-66","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-2-activity","content":"This is Step 2 at work: one meeting refreshed the account, updated a scorecard and created two contacts. Only the stage move is left for a person to confirm."},"5103":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-67","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-3-review","content":"By default, every suggested update surfaces for review before anything is written to the CRM. This is the **Ask First** mode."},"5104":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-68","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-3-review","content":"Watch for the notification. After every activity, CRM Manager sends a message in Slack or your preferred channel saying it found updates for a number of fields, with a link to review them."},"5105":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-69","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-3-review","content":"Open the deal from **Records › Deals** and pick the **CRM Updates** tab. **AI Suggestions** lists each proposed change."},"5106":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-70","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-3-review","content":"Compare the suggested value with the \"Current Value\" line under it."},"5107":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-71","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-3-review","content":"Choose **Accept** or **Reject**."},"5108":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-72","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-3-review","content":"Each suggestion sits above the value it would replace, so reviewing takes a glance. Nothing in the CRM changes until you press Accept."},"5109":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-73","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-3-review","content":"The count beside **AI Suggestions** shows what is waiting on each deal. **AI Updates** lists changes already applied, and **Updates History** keeps the record."},"5110":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-74","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-4-auto-mode","content":"Once accuracy thresholds are met, RevOps confirms the switch to auto mode. In **Auto-Pilot**, unreviewed updates apply automatically, so the pipeline stays current without anyone acting."},"5111":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-75","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-4-auto-mode","content":"On Home, CRM Manager's **Agent Feed** row reports each batch of work. It says how many fields changed, how many applied straight away and how many still need your review."},"5112":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-76","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-4-auto-mode","content":"The feed row is how RevOps watches auto mode without opening every deal. It shows applied and held changes together, so trust builds from real numbers."},"5113":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-77","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-4-auto-mode","content":"Some teams run a weekly review window instead. Reps get their pending suggestions on Friday morning, and on Sunday night they get a confirmation of what was auto-accepted."},"5114":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-78","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-5-monthly-check","content":"Before a board deck or quarterly review, RevOps can check the CRM in one sitting:"},"5115":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-79","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-5-monthly-check","content":"**Read the weekly reports for the month.** Each lists newly created deals, accounts and contacts, fields updated and enriched, and records cleaned or de-duplicated."},"5116":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-80","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-5-monthly-check","content":"**Read the governance digest.** It covers suggestions made, fields updated, reverts, acceptance rate by rep and flags that need review."},"5117":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-81","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-5-monthly-check","content":"**Check the flags.** CRM Manager flags CRM objects with missing or stale data."},"5118":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-82","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-5-monthly-check","content":"**Run a clean-up job.** Ask CRM Manager to work back through old records, for example \"Find all duplicate accounts from last quarter\" or \"Backfill MEDDPICC fields across the pipeline.\""},"5119":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-83","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#step-5-monthly-check","content":"**Chase what's still pending.** Reps get end-of-day reminders for open CRM tasks or unverified updates. If updates stay incomplete past a set window, deals can be deferred or flagged as closed-lost, configured for your org."},"5120":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-84","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#what-it-is","content":"Keeping the CRM updated is the job of Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent. It keeps every object in your CRM accurate, complete and current, without anyone updating records by hand. It isn't a CRM itself: it works on top of Salesforce, HubSpot or Zoho."},"5121":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-85","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#what-it-is","content":"It runs in two modes:"},"5122":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-86","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#what-it-is","content":"| Mode          | When it runs                        | What it does                                                                                                       |\n| ------------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Real-time** | After every meeting, call and email | Syncs updates and fixes duplicate accounts, missing contacts and broken field values as part of the same operation |","table":"table-1"},"5123":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-87","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#what-it-is","content":"| Mode      | When it runs     | What it does                                                                                                    |\n| --------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Batch** | When RevOps asks | Runs jobs across historical data, such as rebuilding broken account hierarchies or cleaning unassigned contacts |","table":"table-1"},"5124":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-88","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#what-it-is","content":"It fills three kinds of fields:"},"5125":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-89","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#what-it-is","content":"| Field type   | Examples                                                       | How it's set up                  |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| **Standard** | Close date, deal amount, stage, next steps, last activity date | Pre-mapped when the CRM connects |","table":"table-2"},"5126":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-90","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#what-it-is","content":"| Field type      | Examples                                                                 | How it's set up                             |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------- |\n| **Methodology** | The framework marked **Active**: MEDDPICC, MEDDIC, SPICED, BANT or DRIVE | Values come from Oliv's Deal Insights layer |","table":"table-2"},"5127":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-91","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#what-it-is","content":"| Field type | Examples                         | How it's set up                         |\n| ---------- | -------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| **Custom** | Any field unique to your process | Mapped by Oliv's team during onboarding |","table":"table-2"},"5128":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-92","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#what-its-for","content":"An updated CRM means the records match what actually happened on calls and in email. Deal stages, close dates and contacts reflect this week, not the last time a rep had a spare hour. Reports built on those fields then mean what they say."},"5129":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-93","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#how-it-helps","content":"**Updates come from conversations.** Fields change because something was said, not because someone remembered to type it."},"5130":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-94","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#how-it-helps","content":"**Each change sits beside the old value.** The suggested value shows above the field's current value."},"5131":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-95","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#how-it-helps","content":"**New people get records.** Contacts and accounts appear when they first show up in a meeting or email."},"5132":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-96","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#how-it-helps","content":"**Old mess gets cleaned too.** Batch jobs work back through duplicates and empty fields from earlier quarters."},"5133":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-97","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#without-it","content":"Without upkeep, the CRM drifts behind the deals it describes. Managers spend 1:1s chasing updates instead of coaching. Pipeline reports run on fields nobody has touched in weeks, and the forecast inherits every gap."},"5134":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-98","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#why-buyers-care","content":"This matters most to revenue operations leads, who own the data and answer for the reports. It also matters to sales and customer success leaders whose reviews depend on current records. It counts most at month and quarter end, when numbers go to leadership."},"5135":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-99","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#approach","content":"Think of a RevOps lead three days before the monthly board deck is due. The pipeline slide pulls straight from the CRM. She needs to trust every close date and stage in it, and she knows some haven't moved in weeks."},"5136":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-100","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#approach","content":"The usual routine is an export to a spreadsheet and a round of messages to reps. Duplicates get merged by hand and blank fields get chased one owner at a time. It tends to eat most of a week, and the clean state often lasts only until the next deck."},"5137":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-101","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#approach","content":"The records drift because updating them is a separate job from selling. Every call already holds the facts the CRM needs. If those facts flow into the fields as calls happen, the end-of-month scramble shrinks to a check."},"5138":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-102","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#approach","content":"Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent does that work after every meeting, call and email. It proposes each change with the suggested value and the current value side by side. Once the team trusts it, RevOps turns on auto mode, and batch jobs clean up older records on request. New contacts, such as a buyer added late to a call, get their own records along the way. Each week's changes then land in one report for RevOps."},"5139":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-103","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#approach","content":"Each suggestion on the deal's **CRM Updates** tab can be accepted or rejected. How other platforms keep CRM fields current is covered in How keeping the CRM updated compares, below."},"5140":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-104","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#with-meeting-follow-up","content":"Oliv AI's Meeting Assistant agent proposes field updates from every call. CRM Manager reviews the same call context and pushes approved changes into the CRM. Account executives see this in their day as part of running deals with Oliv AI, and the next pre-meeting brief starts from the updated record."},"5141":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-105","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#with-deal-driver","content":"Oliv AI's Deal Driver agent raises an alert when a rep hasn't updated the Core 4 Fields after a meeting. It reads the completion data CRM Manager produces. Deal Driver doesn't update fields itself; that stays with CRM Manager."},"5142":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-106","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#with-forecaster","content":"Oliv AI's Forecaster agent uses stage, close date and amount fields for pipeline projections. Clean fields are what make those numbers usable in a board deck. See how teams run evidence-based forecast commits on that data."},"5143":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-107","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#with-tools","content":"Agents that write to Salesforce or HubSpot do it through tools on their **Tools** tab. Agent tools and run modes explains how to make CRM writes wait for approval."},"5144":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-108","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#with-olivia","content":"Oliv AI's Olivia agent can hand field updates and data hygiene work to CRM Manager, one of the specialists she orchestrates. Everything downstream in Oliv AI, from deal scoring to pipeline reviews, is only as good as the data CRM Manager keeps current."},"5145":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-109","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#with-olivia","content":"When Olivia drafts an email for you, her plan for after it goes out names CRM Manager to log the touch on the deal."},"5146":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-110","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#with-olivia","content":"The first item under After this goes out is Log the touch on the deal, attributed to CRM Manager. Emails sent through Olivia reach the CRM without a separate step."},"5147":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-111","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#with-voice","content":"If a meeting wasn't recorded, CRM Manager can prompt the rep by voice (Beta). The rep gives a quick spoken summary, and CRM Manager uses it as a source."},"5148":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-112","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#who-uses-it","content":"These are typical patterns, shown to illustrate how teams use CRM Manager."},"5149":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-113","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#revenue-operations","content":"A RevOps lead starts on **Ask First**, watches acceptance rates by rep in the weekly digest, and confirms auto mode once they hold up. Monthly, she runs a duplicate check and a methodology backfill before reporting. It's how RevOps teams run autonomous agents across the process."},"5150":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-114","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#account-executives","content":"An account executive finishes a demo where a new economic buyer joined late. By the next call, the contact is in the CRM, the stakeholder role is set and the next step is logged. The rep reviews the updates in Slack instead of typing them up, much like AI sales call notes save the write-up."},"5151":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-115","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#sales-managers","content":"A sales manager checks the **AI Suggestions** count on each deal's **CRM Updates** tab before a 1:1. Deals with a pile of unreviewed updates are the ones to raise first. The sales manager's daily guide shows the rest of the routine."},"5152":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-116","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#customer-success","content":"A customer success manager's QBRs and check-in calls update account records too. When a champion mentions a reorg in passing, the stakeholder map changes and the champion is flagged at risk. CRM Manager covers renewals and CS check-ins, not just new sales."},"5153":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-117","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare","content":"Oliv AI proposes each CRM change for review first, then lets RevOps switch to automatic updates once they're trusted. It creates new contacts from activity and sends RevOps a weekly report of what changed. Oliv AI is the only platform in this table that does all four."},"5154":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-118","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare","content":"CRM updates, from each platform's public documentation:"},"5155":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-119","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare","content":"| Platform    | Proposed updates you review first | Automatic updates once trusted | New contacts created from activity | Weekly CRM-change report for RevOps |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| **Oliv AI** | Yes                               | Yes                            | Yes                                | Yes                                 |","table":"table-3"},"5156":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-120","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare","content":"| Platform | Proposed updates you review first      | Automatic updates once trusted     | New contacts created from activity | Weekly CRM-change report for RevOps |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| **Gong** | Partly (one text field on deal boards) | Yes (AI data fields mapped to CRM) | Doesn't create Salesforce contacts | Not in docs                         |","table":"table-3"},"5157":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-121","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare","content":"| Platform     | Proposed updates you review first      | Automatic updates once trusted | New contacts created from activity | Weekly CRM-change report for RevOps |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| **Outreach** | Yes (reviewable field recommendations) | Yes (auto update per field)    | Not in docs                        | Not in docs                         |","table":"table-3"},"5158":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-122","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare","content":"| Platform         | Proposed updates you review first    | Automatic updates once trusted | New contacts created from activity       | Weekly CRM-change report for RevOps |\n| ---------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| **Fireflies.ai** | Yes (nothing sent until you approve) | Not in docs                    | Yes (new HubSpot contacts from meetings) | Not in docs                         |","table":"table-3"},"5159":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-123","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare","content":"| Platform  | Proposed updates you review first | Automatic updates once trusted    | New contacts created from activity   | Weekly CRM-change report for RevOps |\n| --------- | --------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |\n| **Avoma** | Not in docs                       | Yes (sync without manual updates) | Yes (contacts created from meetings) | Not in docs                         |","table":"table-3"},"5160":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-124","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare","content":"| Platform   | Proposed updates you review first | Automatic updates once trusted        | New contacts created from activity | Weekly CRM-change report for RevOps |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| **Fathom** | Not in docs                       | Yes (summaries written to Salesforce) | Not in docs                        | Not in docs                         |","table":"table-3"},"5161":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-125","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare","content":"*Yes: documented and built in. Partly: documented with a limit, shown in brackets. Not in docs: not found in the vendor's public documentation.*"},"5162":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-126","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare-stronger","content":"**New people get CRM records.** Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent creates the record when an activity involves a company or person not yet in the CRM. Gong's Salesforce FAQ says Gong doesn't create contacts in Salesforce. See Oliv AI as a Gong alternative."},"5163":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-127","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare-stronger","content":"**Review first, then let it run.** Oliv AI starts every update in review and moves to auto mode once accuracy holds. Fireflies.ai says nothing is sent to Salesforce until you review and approve it."},"5164":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-128","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare-stronger","content":"**A weekly account of what changed.** Oliv AI sends RevOps a weekly report of records created, fields updated and records cleaned. Avoma documents automating field updates to manage your pipeline. See Oliv AI vs Avoma."},"5165":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-129","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare-stronger","content":"**Clean-up across past records.** Oliv AI runs batch jobs across historical data on request. Fathom's Salesforce guide lists retroactive sync as manual, one call at a time. See Gong vs Oliv AI."},"5166":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-130","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#compare-stronger","content":"*Competitor details checked against each vendor's public documentation on 21 October 2026. Features and plans change, so confirm with the vendor before you decide.*"},"5167":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-131","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#limits","content":"**Three CRMs out of the box.** Salesforce, HubSpot and Zoho are supported. Other CRMs are available on request."},"5168":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-132","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#limits","content":"**Custom fields need onboarding.** Oliv's team maps them during onboarding; until then, CRM Manager fills standard and methodology fields."},"5169":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-133","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#limits","content":"**Review comes first.** By default every update waits for review. Auto mode starts only when RevOps confirms it."},"5170":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-134","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#limits","content":"**Field values come from Deal Insights.** CRM Manager writes what Oliv's Deal Insights layer produces. It doesn't score deals or decide values from scratch."},"5171":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-135","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#limits","content":"**Not a reporting tool.** It makes your existing reports accurate but doesn't replace them."},"5172":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-136","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#limits","content":"**Not a deal-risk tool.** Pipeline risk signals belong to Oliv AI's Deal Driver agent."},"5173":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-137","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#limits","content":"**Pending updates have consequences.** Depending on your org's settings, deals with overdue updates can be deferred or flagged as closed-lost."},"5174":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-138","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#limits","content":"**Voice prompts are Beta.** Spoken summaries for unrecorded meetings are part of the Voice Agent (Beta)."},"5175":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-139","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-clean-crm","content":"No. Real-time mode fixes issues as new activity comes in, and batch mode cleans what's already there. CRM Manager is built to start on messy data."},"5176":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-140","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-direct-write","content":"Both ways are possible. By default, every suggested update surfaces for review first. Once your team trusts it, switch to auto mode for hands-free updates."},"5177":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-141","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-wrong-update","content":"Each suggestion shows the field's current value beside the suggested one, so you can reject it before it's written. **Updates History** keeps the record of what changed."},"5178":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-142","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-crms","content":"Salesforce, HubSpot and Zoho out of the box. Additional CRMs are available on request."},"5179":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-143","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-custom-fields","content":"Oliv's team, during onboarding, as a service. Once mapped, custom fields update the same way as standard and methodology fields."},"5180":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-144","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-hierarchy","content":"Yes. CRM Manager maps parent and subsidiary accounts and keeps them current as org structures change. A full hierarchy rebuild can run in batch mode."},"5181":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-145","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-customer-success","content":"Yes. It tracks activity across sales cycles, renewals, QBRs and customer success check-ins."},"5182":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-146","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-weekly-report","content":"A report of newly created deals, accounts and contacts, fields updated and enriched, and records cleaned or de-duplicated. A governance digest adds acceptance rate by rep and flags that need review."},"5183":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-147","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-pending","content":"Yes. The count beside **AI Suggestions** on each deal's **CRM Updates** tab shows what's waiting."},"5184":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-148","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#faq-field-history","content":"Yes. Each deal's **CRM Updates** tab has an **Updates History** list of the changes made."},"5185":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-149","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"Agent tools and run modes: make CRM writes wait for approval."},"5186":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-150","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"Oliv AI product documentation: every guide, by agent and feature."},"5187":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-151","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"Deal Driver agent guide: manager alerts that read CRM completion data."},"5188":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-152","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"Olivia agent guide: the agent that hands work to specialists such as CRM Manager."},"5189":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-153","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"Prepare for a meeting: briefs built from current CRM records."},"5190":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-154","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"Account executive guide to running deals: where reps review CRM updates day to day."},"5191":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-155","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"Context graph and your CRM: how Oliv AI enriches records without replacing your CRM."},"5192":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-156","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"AI for revenue operations: how scaling teams use AI across RevOps."},"5193":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-157","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"AI agents for RevOps: forecasting, routing and deal work handed to agents."},"5194":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-158","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"Sales reporting software: reports that depend on current CRM fields."},"5195":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated-159","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/keep-the-crm-updated#related","content":"Fixing CRM sync issues: what goes wrong when sync breaks."},"5196":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting","type":"page","content":"Prepare for a meeting","breadcrumbs":["Oliv AI docs","Workflows"],"tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting"},"5197":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting-0","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting","content":"How Oliv AI prepares you for a sales meeting, from the deal brief that arrives 30 minutes before the call to first-meeting research on a new contact, and how to use both."},"5198":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting-1","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance"},"5199":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting-2","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"5200":{"id":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meeting-3","page_id":"/product-docs/workflows/prepare-for-a-meetin