er shows the present value beside each proposal. Gong's extractor notes that when new or better information is found, the previous value is overwritten. See Oliv AI as a Gong alternative."],[4387,"**Review changes** shows each affected file as a line-by-line diff, then lists the knock-on effects. You choose **Approve & merge**, **Request edit** or **Cancel**, and an approved change shows as **Merged**. A minor update, such as syncing an agent prompt to a scorecard, can apply as **Autonomous**. The **History** tab logs it as \"No human review needed\". More on how that works is on the Oliver agent page."],[5169,"**Review comes first.** By default every update waits for review. Auto mode starts only when RevOps confirms it."],[3725,"**Review first, automate later.** Ask First shows each update beside the current value, and RevOps decides when to switch to Auto-Pilot. Gong documents that AI Data Extractor runs automatically, with no action from reps. See Oliv AI as a Gong alternative."],[5163,"**Review first, then let it run.** Oliv AI starts every update in review and moves to auto mode once accuracy holds. Fireflies.ai says nothing is sent to Salesforce until you review and approve it."],[3731,"**Review is the default.** Auto-Pilot starts only after RevOps confirms the switch."],[4715,"**Review is the default.** Auto-Pilot starts only after RevOps confirms the switch."],[1781,"**Review it.** **Review changes** shows each file as a diff, with removed lines in red and added lines in green. Cards below list the knock-on effects, such as a new CRM field, an agent retrained or deals re-scored."],[969,"**Review updates as they arrive.** Reps check suggestions while the team builds confidence in them."],[519,"**Risk is set where it lives.** A record lookup and a stage update on the same agent can run under different modes."],[1906,"**Risk raised early.** She flags deals with no activity, close dates nearing without progress, or qualification gaps."],[1260,"**Risk shows up early.** Alerts fire the moment deals stall or stages drift, not when a rep escalates."],[5616,"**Risk shows up early.** Alerts fire when deals stall or stages drift, not when a rep finally mentions it."],[4316,"**Role examples are a guide.** Assign by the apps a person needs, not by job title alone."],[521,"**Routine reads stay quick.** **Auto Run** lets low-risk actions happen without a prompt."],[3206,"**Rules come before scale.** Managers get alerts and forecasts that follow one agreed process."],[5118,"**Run a clean-up job.** Ask CRM Manager to work back through old records, for example \"Find all duplicate accounts from last quarter\" or \"Backfill MEDDPICC fields across the pipeline.\""],[4805,"**Run history** is the record of every time the agent has worked."],[4437,"**Run records are read-only.** A record shows what a run did. Approval happens in the review step, not in the record."],[3368,"**Run records hand off to Gmail.** An agent's run record shows one card per contact under an **Email Sent** banner, with the **To** chip, **Subject** and full body. **Open in Gmail** opens Gmail's compose screen with the recipient, subject and body filled in. It doesn't send anything."],[2847,"**Run the call.** Once connected, the card switches to **Record call**, a **Recording method** of **One-way** or **Two-way**, pause, mute and **End Call**."],[721,"**Runs don't name their trigger.** The run history says a run was **Auto-triggered**, not which trigger or schedule started it."],[4827,"**Sales development** uses agents to find, qualify and engage the right buyers faster."],[1743,"**Sales methodology.** MEDDPICC, BANT, SPICED or a custom framework, and the fields each stage requires."],[3591,"**Salesforce.** A Salesforce admin installs the package for all users. The Salesforce setup guide covers the install, review settings and cleaning up existing data."],[1757,"**Same rules for every rep.** Two reps can't track different data points on the same type of opportunity."],