eal**."],[3238,"**Some steps need an admin.** Salesforce, Zoom recording without the host and, in some workspaces, Slack all need an admin on your side."],[2535,"**Someone outside organized it.** A note taker joins as a visible participant, shown with your company's name. If the meeting has a waiting room or lobby, admit it so recording can begin."],[4093,"**Someone outside your company organized it.** The note taker joins as a visible participant, shown with your company's name. If the meeting has a waiting room, someone may need to admit it."],[275,"**Spreadsheets and data files too.** Oliv AI's upload area names .csv, json, xlsx and xls beside .pdf, docx and .pptx. Outreach's guidance covers knowledge documents such as product brochures, persona guides and battle cards. See how Gong and Outreach compare."],[5490,"**Stage moves wait for you.** A change of deal stage stays a **Pending Update** until you confirm it. Other updates, such as a refreshed account summary or a new contact, show on the **CRM Updates** tab once written."],[943,"**Stakeholder roles.** It tracks each contact's role on each opportunity, such as economic buyer, champion or blocker, and updates Opportunity Contact Roles."],[3490,"**Stakeholders on the record.** Every new person from a call becomes a contact with a role on the deal."],[4906,"**Stakeholders.** Who is in the meeting, what roles they play and what they care about, based on prior conversations."],[1598,"**Stakeholders.** Who's in the meeting, the role each plays, and what they care about based on earlier conversations."],[988,"**Stale data flags.** CRM objects with missing or stale data."],[4895,"**Stalls flagged early.** You get a nudge when next steps go overdue or activity drops."],[3546,"**Standard fields from day one.** Core deal properties are pre-mapped on connection and fill from day one. Avoma lists a HubSpot Business license for users of field mapping. Compare Oliv AI vs Avoma."],[3661,"**Standard fields.** Close date, deal amount, stage, next steps and last activity date are pre-mapped when you connect, and populate from day one."],[1093,"**Standard fields.** Close date, deal amount, stage, next steps and last activity date. These are pre-mapped and fill from day one."],[948,"**Standard fields.** Close date, deal amount, stage, next steps and last activity date. These are pre-mapped when you connect your CRM."],[2843,"**Start a session.** Click **New Session**. On the **Power Dialer** page, pick a **List**, which shows its prospect count, and a **Call using** number, then click **Start a Session**."],[4428,"**Start CRM updates on Ask First.** Reps accept or reject each suggestion for the first weeks."],[714,"**Started by a deal event, not only the clock.** Oliv AI's Multithreader agent fires when a deal's stage is set to Proposal. Avoma's scheduled prompts run a question on a recurring basis. See Avoma vs Oliv AI."],[105,"**Steps lead to tools.** Pressing a tool chip opens that tool and its approval setting."],[148,"**Steps tied to the tools they use.** Oliv AI draws each tool as a chip inside the step that uses it. Outreach's Deal Agent starts MEDDPICC users on pre-defined fields and prompts. See how Gong and Outreach compare."],[1392,"**Submissions.** Each person's number per measurement and period, with **Deals Sum**, **Last Week** and **Roll-Up** beside it. **My Team** shows how many rows each person has submitted, and the header shows the **Due Date**."],[439,"**Success** and **Sent** on most agents. An agent that drafts replies adds **Draft ready** and **No reply needed**. A sequence shows the step reached, such as **Completed Step 2**, then **Escalated to CSM** or **Sequence Completed**."],[360,"**Success** or **Sent**, for a finished run;"],[5492,"**Summary messages can be turned off.** If you'd rather not get the Slack and email summaries, disable them on your **Profile Settings** page."],[2529,"**Summary of tomorrow's meetings.** Sent at 4 PM local time, it lists the meetings Oliv AI will summarize the next day."],[5605,"**Sunset Summary.** Every weekday evening, Deal Driver recaps wins, risks and next-step gaps: deals won or lost, meetings held and their outcomes, deals newly flagged at risk and open situations to follow up. It also notes whether the day's meetings were recorded."],[1248,"**Sunset Summary.** Sent every weekday as an end-of-day recap of wins, risks and next-step gaps. Its Overview covers meetings, deal progress, notable updates and customer engagement."],[3235,"**Support that sets things up.** Oliv AI's onboarding team builds the handbook with your revenue operations lead. Avoma documents a designated customer success manager on its Organization and Enterprise plans. See Oliv AI vs Avoma."],[4432,"**Switch to auto per area.** When accuracy thresholds are met, RevOps confirms the move to Auto-Pilot."],[970,"**Switch to auto when you're ready.** Once accuracy thresholds are met, RevOps confirms the move to auto mode."],[2806,"**Switch views.** **Active** shows open conversations with a count, and **Completed** holds finished ones. **Search** and **Filters** narrow either view."],[3234,"**Tailored on day one.** Oliv AI tailors its signal models within 1 day of the proof of value kickoff. Gong documents AI trackers that you write and publish yourself. See Oliv AI as a Gong alternative."],[2830,"**Target Level.** Choose **Company**, where messaging varies by persona and a play can use several flows, or **Contact**, which targets one person with a single flow."],[3185,"**Targets.** In **Settings › Targets**, click **Create Target**, assign the users it applies to and track **Overall Progress**. Finished targets move to **Completed Targets**."],[4922,"**Tasks from next steps.** It creates tasks from the next steps in meetings, calls and emails, and assigns them to the right owner."],[3486,"**Tasks.** Next steps from meetings, calls and emails become tasks assigned to the right owner."],[1811,"**Tell it, don't configure it.** RevOps describes a process change to Oliver in plain language. Gong's playbooks are built in AI Deal Reviewer settings, with up to 20 elements per playbook. Compare Oliv AI vs Gong."],[3198,"**Tell Oliver what changed.** Anything you learned in the month goes to Oliver as a process update. It waits as **Pending Review** until you approve it, then every connected agent picks it up."],[4114,"**Tell the Oliv team.** They finish the remaining setup on the backend."],[99,"**Templates.** An output can give the exact message the agent sends, with placeholders such as `{{deal_name}}`."],[1747,"**Territory and segmentation rules.** How pipeline is divided, and who owns what."],[1305,"**The 1:1 report comes to you.** Deal Driver compiles each rep's pipeline on that rep's own schedule and files it in the manager's My Reports. Gong recommends checking a deal board weekly, particularly before 1:1s and pipeline reviews. Compare Oliv AI vs Gong."],[3405,"**The calendar comes first.** Calendar integration is required. Without it, Oliv can't take notes in your meetings."],[3237,"**The calendar comes first.** Oliv AI can't take notes in meetings until calendars are connected, so that step can't be skipped or delayed."],[3817,"**The call is summed up at once.** The meeting summary is sent as soon as the meeting ends."],[428,"**The cause isn't named.** A run is marked automatic without saying which trigger or schedule started it."],[3344,"**The CRM catches up by itself.** Contact roles and tasks are updated from signals in emails, as well as calls and meetings."],[1615,"**The CRM keeps pace.** Changes heard on the call come back as CRM updates you can check on the meeting."],[5455,"**The CRM keeps up.** Field updates are proposed from what was said, ready to approve."],[1259,"**The day starts briefed.** Meetings, risks and deals that need attention first are surfaced before the day starts."],[3550,"**The deal card is yours to add.** Oliv AI fields show on the deal view once you create the property and card in HubSpot."],[5453,"**The draft is waiting.** The follow-up is written within minutes of the call ending."],[1614,"**The email is already written.** The draft comes from the real conversation, so you edit rather than start from a blank page."],[2057,"**The exact moment, found.** You search for the objection or pricing concern, then clip it into a library."],[1460,"**The forecast is built before anyone logs in.** Forecaster pre-drafts each rep's forecast, so reps review and submit in minutes. In Gong, a panel opens where you submit your number for the selected category. Compare Oliv AI vs Gong."],[2194,"**The full context.** A link back to the source recording."],[2416,"**The full transcript travels with the summary.** Oliv AI attaches the AI summary and the full call transcript to the opportunity record. Avoma documents pushing meeting notes, action items, and insights to the CRM. See Gong vs Avoma for where Oliv AI fits."],[2348,"**The gist in a minute.** Key takeaways and the AI summary are ready as soon as the call ends."],[858,"**The goal is tracked every week.** Once the manager sets a goal, Coach sends the rep a weekly report on wins, the remaining gap and one focus. Avoma sends coaching recommendations as Slack alerts, with its Revenue Intelligence add-on. Compare Oliv AI vs Avoma."],[808,"**The goal stays visible.** A weekly report keeps it in front of the rep between conversations."],[4097,"**The host can be late.** With a Zoom admin's permission, recording goes ahead even if the host never joins."],[2554,"**The link arrives without anyone sharing it.** Each Oliv AI meeting message carries **Open Meeting** automatically. Avoma documents a way to share the meeting link directly to a Slack channel or DM. Compare Oliv AI vs Avoma."],[1658,"**The manager gets the call context without asking.** Before every 1:1, Meeting Assistant summarizes what happened on each call. Outreach's manager workflows suggest you use pipeline summary to review a rep's opportunities and pull that context together yourself. Read how Gong and Outreach compare."],[103,"**The method is in writing.** **Process** lists every step in order, with a title and a description."],[4010,"**The note taker joins external calls automatically.** If a call shouldn't be captured, remove the note taker for that call ahead of time."],[3809,"**The Oliv Slack app.** Install it at web.oliv.ai/slack/direct-install."],[2702,"**The organizer decides, not you.** You can't force botless recording on a meeting someone outside your company organized. Send the invite yourself if it matters."],[2507,"**The outcome at a glance.** Each row shows the next step and the start of the AI summary."],[230,"**The Overview shows it too.** Knowledge pills tell you what background an agent has before you open it."],[4404,"**The people it touched.** A **Top Identified Contacts** panel lists them."],[1759,"**The playbook learns.** Oliver spots patterns across deals and drafts the next update for you."],[227,"**The reading list is visible.** **Knowledge in use** names every file an agent has."],[2814,"**The reason, shown.** Every account shows why it sits where it does. The **Signal** column names the trigger and how many days ago it happened."],[2110,"**The recording method is chosen for you.** Oliv AI records botlessly when your company hosts and joins visibly when someone else does. Avoma's setup asks you to choose Cloud Recording or the Avoma Assistant bot. Compare Oliv AI vs Avoma."],[5332,"**The research brief is short by design.** It's three bullets and an icebreaker. The full detail view is in the platform."],[4643,"**The right deal on busy accounts.** Activity is matched even when one account has several open opportunities."],[3400,"**The right deal, not just the account.** Oliv AI matches email to the right opportunity when an account has several. In Gong's Salesforce logging, the account is used when several opportunities could match. Compare Oliv AI vs Gong."],[4708,"**The right deal, not just the right account.** Oliv AI matches activity to the right opportunity when one account has several open. Gong documents that with multiple opportunities, the Related to field gets the account. Compare Oliv AI vs Gong."],[4921,"**The right deal.** It maps each activity to the right account and opportunity, including multi-threaded deals. If it can't resolve one, it asks you."],[1394,"**The submission drawer.** One person's commit, built as **Commit** plus **Adjustment**, with comments and what moved since the last snapshot. Its deal tabs are **Committed Deals**, **Closed Won Deals**, **Most Likely Deals**, **Best Case Deals** and **Pipeline Deals**."],[4818,"**The web app.** Home, agents, apps, reports, records, activities, the playbook and settings live here."],[2349,"**The words, not a paraphrase.** Timestamps link each point back to the moment in the recording."],[5167,"**Three CRMs out of the box.** Salesforce, HubSpot and Zoho are supported. Other CRMs are available on request."],[4712,"**Three CRMs out of the box.** Salesforce, HubSpot and Zoho connect directly. Any other CRM is a request to Oliv AI's team."],[3815,"**Tomorrow is planned today.** At 4 PM local time, you see every meeting Oliv will summarize the next day."],[2553,"**Tomorrow's meetings, in Slack, the day before.** Oliv AI sends the list at 4 PM local time. Gong's daily digest is an email for team members with calls that day. Compare Oliv AI vs Gong."],[3867,"**Tomorrow's plan, in Slack.** Oliv posts the next day's meetings at 4 PM local time. Gong's daily digest is an email that may include a personalized schedule of upcoming calls. Compare Oliv AI vs Gong."],[577,"**Tools can't be removed or reordered.** There's no delete control on a tool card or in the sidebar."],[578,"**Tools have no settings of their own.** There are no parameters, field mappings or filters, so you can't limit a tool to certain records or fields."],[4802,"**Tools** are the actions the agent may take, such as looking up a record or drafting an email."],[126,"**Top-level entries**, such as **Objective**, **Process** and **Output**, appear in darker, heavier text. Pressing one scrolls to that section."],[2422,"**Transcript sharing starts at a minute marker.** A shared segment plays from the minute marker you picked."],[4803,"**Triggers and schedules** start an agent on auto-pilot, from an event or at a fixed time."],[3207,"**Trust is earned.** CRM updates start in review, and auto mode waits until the numbers say so."],[3830,"**Turn messages off if you prefer.** You can disable the automated messages from your **Profile Settings** page, the last item in the **Settings** menu."],[2088,"**Turn on botless recording.** If it isn't set up for your organization, contact Oliv Support and connect your video conferencing admin with them."],[3874,"**Turning them off is one place.** Disable the automated messages from your **Profile Settings** page."],[2250,"**Two access types.** A library is either **Public** or **Private**."],[4434,"**Two controls, two places.** Tool run modes are set per tool on each agent. The conversation setting is set per conversation with Olivia or Oliver. Changing one leaves the other as it was."],[3407,"**Unclear cases go to the seller.** When CRM Manager can't resolve where an email belongs, it asks the seller."],[3732,"**Unclear matches go back to people.** If an activity can't be matched to the right account or opportunity, the rep is asked."],[4556,"**Unclear matches go to a person.** When Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent can't resolve where an activity belongs, it asks the seller."],[5129,"**Updates come from conversations.** Fields change because something was said, not because someone remembered to type it."],[3544,"**Updates follow each activity.** Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent proposes changes after every meeting, call and email and notifies the rep. Gong's help center notes that exporting Gong data to HubSpot can take up to six hour