ne for briefs and follow-ups. Portfolio Manager's 1:1 briefings follow once recordings and CRM data are flowing."],[3532,"A head of sales opens the deals board on Monday and finds stages, amounts and next steps already updated from last week's calls. The **AI Suggestions** count on each deal's **CRM Updates** tab shows what still needs review. More on Oliv AI for sales managers."],[1280,"A high-value opportunity goes quiet."],[5583,"A high-value opportunity goes quiet."],[1443,"A manager doesn't have to open the board to learn that the forecast moved: Forecaster reports overnight category shifts in the Agent Feed."],[2543,"A manager opens **Team meetings** before a 1:1 and reads each rep's next steps down the column. Then they open one meeting to coach from what happened. See Oliv AI for sales managers."],[2405,"A manager reads **Meeting insights** and **Coaching** before a 1:1. An enablement lead clips a strong objection handle for onboarding. Read about sales enablement software."],[2858,"A manager sets each play's priority, watches its stage cards and checks which experiments to promote. Each account shows its signal and fit, so a coaching conversation starts from the account, not from activity counts. For the call side of coaching, see Oliv AI's Coach agent."],[4925,"A meeting's **Action Items** tab shows the **Next meeting**, **Next action** and **Next follow-up**, then the tasks from the call with an assignee and a due date. Each task links to the moment in the recording it came from."],[4384,"A meeting's own **CRM Updates** tab lists what was written after the call, such as a refreshed account summary or a new contact. A bigger change, such as a stage move, waits as **Pending Update** until you press **Update Deal**."],[2198,"A moment is a description of what to capture. Each moment routes to one library and one Slack channel. Three moment types come ready: **Product Requests**, **Competitor Mentions** and **Objections**. You can add your own, for example dis