."],[5668,"Deal Driver agent guide: every alert, brief and report the agent sends."],[5187,"Deal Driver agent guide: manager alerts that read CRM completion data."],[448,"Deal Driver agent guide: pipeline alerts and 1:1 reports for managers."],[169,"Deal Driver agent: how Oliv AI's Deal Driver agent works on open deals."],[293,"Deal Driver agent: how Oliv AI's Deal Driver agent works on open deals."],[733,"Deal Driver agent: how Oliv AI's Deal Driver agent works on open deals."],[4457,"Deal Driver agent: risk alerts grounded in your qualification framework."],[1283,"Deal Driver also nudges reps directly when deals stall, next steps go overdue or activity drops. That catches the gap before a manager needs to step in."],[4056,"Deal Driver and Coach"],[905,"Deal Driver and Forecaster"],[3302,"Deal Driver and Forecaster"],[3625,"Deal Driver and Forecaster"],[4600,"Deal Driver and Forecaster"],[5575,"Deal Driver compiles a structured view of each rep's pipeline before their 1:1. In **My Reports**, open **One-on-One Prep** and pick the rep. The report shows their total pipeline and deal count, then a **Pipeline Summary** of **Pipeline Health**, **Deal Momentum** and **Areas for Improvement**."],[1242,"Deal Driver is also a bundle. It includes the capabilities of Oliv AI's Meeting Assistant agent: pre-call prep, post-call follow-up and CRM sync for reps. If you're on Deal Driver, your reps already have Meeting Assistant."],[1264,"Deal Driver is bought by sales managers, VPs of Sales and regional heads. The sales manager is the main daily beneficiary, because the agent turns time spent on admin into time spent coaching."],[1276,"Deal Driver monitors all activity and triggers an alert when:"],[1324,"Deal Driver on oliv.ai: the agent's own page, with its weekly cadence."],[3918,"Deal Driver, Coach and Content Curator"],[3777,"Deal Driver, Coach and Forecaster"],[1243,"Deal Driver's reports sit together under one card in My Reports, each with its schedule. Pipeline Review is the Monday view of every deal, grouped by status, for leadership updates."],[1328,"Deal intelligence explained: how AI predicts pipeline risk."],[5675,"Deal intelligence software: how AI predicts pipeline risk."],[1205,"Deal risk alerts and next steps"],[4963,"Deal tracking software: use cases and what to weigh."],[59,"Deal work"],[614,"Deal work that starts from a stage"],[4933,"Deal workflow features for account executives, from each platform's public documentation:"],[4591,"Decide how Oliv AI writes to the CRM"],[3444,"Decide how updates are approved"],[901,"Direct a clean-up job"],[4757,"Do agents act without my approval?"],[4368,"Do agents learn from my corrections?"],[4875,"Do CRM updates go in without me seeing them?"],[1071,"Do custom fields update differently from standard fields?"],[2769,"Do I approve outreach before it goes out?"],[5067,"Do I need a clean CRM before I start?"],[5233,"Do I need a clean CRM before the brief works?"],[4483,"Do I need a clean CRM before the context graph works?"],[2617,"Do I need an integration for Teams or Google Meet?"],[3929,"Do I need an Oliv account first?"],[4067,"Do I need both Zoom apps?"],[1228,"Do I need Meeting Assistant separately?"],[3315,"Do I need to connect my calendar?"],[4612,"Do I need to replace Salesforce or HubSpot?"],[4755,"Do I need to replace Salesforce or HubSpot?"],[3789,"Do I need to set anything up after connecting Slack?"],[2483,"Do I need to set up these messages?"],[1077,"Do meeting notes go to the CRM too?"],[3464,"Do reps have to approve every change?"],[1232,"Do reps need to change how they work?"],[5548,"Do reps need to do anything differently?"],[3123,"Do reps need training?"],[3126,"Do the models keep up after launch?"],[4236,"Do viewers and admins need a Sell or Grow seat?"],[3460,"Do we have to move off HubSpot to use Oliv AI?"],[1725,"Do we have to run Oliver ourselves?"],[3120,"Do we need to clean the CRM before we start?"],[4245,"Do we need to replace Salesforce or HubSpot?"],[4239,"Does a higher plan include the lower ones?"],[781,"Does Coach replace Deal Driver?"],[776,"Does Coach work for BDRs?"],[918,"Does CRM Manager write directly to my CRM, or do I approve updates first?"],[5068,"Does CRM Manager write directly to my CRM?"],[1229,"Does Deal Driver write to the CRM?"],[2770,"Does Engage include a dialer?"],[2773,"Does Engage replace my CRM?"],[4623,"Does every agent write to the CRM?"],[1379,"Does Forecaster send anything to managers?"],[1578,"Does it change CRM fields on its own?"],[924,"Does it cover customer success, or just sales?"],[4877,"Does it create contacts I haven't added?"],[926,"Does it create new contacts?"],[3644,"Does it log activity from meetings Oliv AI didn't record?"],[925,"Does it only log meetings that Oliv AI joined?"],[5072,"Does it understand account hierarchies?"],[923,"Does it understand account hierarchy?"],[1225,"Does it work for BDR teams?"],[5546,"Does it work for BDR teams?"],[3469,"Does it work for customer calls after the sale?"],[5073,"Does it work for customer success as well as sales?"],[1230,"Does it work for customer success managers?"],[1575,"Does it work for every meeting, or only some?"],[4076,"Does it work for Microsoft Teams and Google Meet too?"],[3937,"Does it work for Zoom, Teams and Google Meet as well?"],[5392,"Does it work if the customer hosted the meeting?"],[2171,"Does it work on customer success and onboarding calls?"],[3799,"Does it work with Microsoft Teams instead?"],[3324,"Does it work with Outlook instead?"],[2322,"Does Oliv AI detect competitor mentions?"],[4486,"Does Oliv AI keep the content of calls and emails, or only metadata?"],[4365,"Does Oliv AI know who said what on a call?"],[4493,"Does Oliv AI pull in product usage and billing data?"],[2965,"Does Oliv AI replace my CRM?"],[3637,"Does Oliv AI replace Salesforce?"],[2029,"Does Oliv AI send a bot to every meeting?"],[3647,"Does Oliv AI work with other CRMs?"],[4070,"Does Oliv record without asking?"],[3933,"Does Oliv send reminders for Webex meetings?"],[1719,"Does Oliver change things on its own?"],[3322,"Does Olivia read my email?"],[1881,"Does Olivia work in Slack?"],[2771,"Does Prospector send emails without the rep?"],[1883,"Does she really watch my conversations?"],[4618,"Does Slack and email activity reach the CRM?"],[2165,"Does the agent clip automatically, or do I trigger it?"],[4366,"Does the AI read whole calls or snippets?"],[5232,"Does the brief include an agenda?"],[2034,"Does the call record reach my CRM?"],[1371,"Does the forecast roll up through more than one manager?"],[2767,"Does the list update on its own?"],[2326,"Does the meeting reach my CRM?"],[775,"Does the rep see the monthly review?"],[2319,"Does the transcript show who said what?"],[1373,"Does this replace my CRM forecast field?"],[474,"Drafted emails and run records"],[3296,"Drafts and replies in Gmail"],[1856,"Drafts that wait for your choice"],[246,"Drag files onto the dashed area marked \"Drag & drop or choose files to upload.\""],[251,"Drag-and-drop needs a mouse or trackpad. The **choose files** link works without one."],[5599,"Drilling in narrows the board to one manager's team, which is the view a first-line manager walks through rep by rep."],[2849,"During a call the plan stays on screen, so the rep can follow it while recording, pausing or muting. The figures in the plan shown are sample data, not results."],[4312,"During a proof of concept, Oliv AI estimates agent spend at your expected volume. It then assesses return on investment against time saved and business value before rollout. Custom agents you build follow the same model; agent tools and run modes covers what an agent can do in connected apps."],[5005,"During and after the call"],[1823,"During onboarding, Oliv AI's team works with your RevOps lead to populate the first handbook. It typically takes 1 to 2 weeks."],[2789,"Each **play** opens on its own detail page, with its own tabs and an **Edit Play** button."],[4507,"Each activity keeps its full content. An email, call, calendar event or Slack message is captured as a rich context object with participants, content and timestamps, not just its metadata."],[3272,"Each agent posts its work to the **Agent Feed**, which you can filter by team, role, agent and time."],[1282,"Each alert includes the deal, the signal, the relevant context and a suggested action for the manager."],[1413,"Each board keeps weekly snapshots and an end-of-quarter snapshot, so any commit can be reopened as it stood and checked against what actually closed. How that learning loop lines up against other forecasting tools is covered in How the Forecaster agent compares, below."],[1421,"Each cadence ties a board to a rhythm, such as reps every Friday and managers every Monday, which is the schedule Forecaster collects and drafts against."],[3189,"Each cadence ties a board to submission days for reps and managers, so the Forecaster knows when to ask each role for their number."],[4896,"Each call can cost 15 to 20 minutes of digging for context beforehand and about 15 minutes of email writing afterward. CRM updates depend on what the rep remembers. Qualification gaps then surface at the forecast review, when it's too late to act on them."],[2380,"Each card also shows talk time, engagement and **Key Attendee Insights** with timestamps. **View Contact** opens the person's full contact record."],[2840,"Each Engage seat includes one connected primary mailbox and LinkedIn automation. You manage your sending setup from the same workspace as your sequences and follow-ups. When a team needs more volume, you add more warm email mailboxes. For outreach strategy, see the guide to outbound sales software."],[3693,"Each meeting also has a **CRM Updates** tab. It shows what was written after the call, such as **Account Updated**, **Opportunity Updated** or **Contact Created**, and holds a stage move as a **Pending Update** until someone presses **Update Deal**."],[2346,"Each meeting also has a shared view, opened by link at an address of the form `/meeting/view/<id>`. It's for someone who needs to see the meeting from outside your Oliv AI workspace."],[5307,"Each meeting card in the brief has **Add me to this call**, **Leave a note** and **Review Deal**, and a line comparing the meeting with your own calendar. Deal Driver also prepares a **One-on-One Prep** report for each rep, on that rep's own day, such as every Thursday or every Friday. Oliv AI's Coach agent follows minutes later with that rep's coaching goal."],[5573,"Each meeting card shows the meeting type and time, checks it against your calendar, and offers **Add me to this call** and **Leave a note**. On review day, the important meetings and priority deals are a good first cut of the agenda."],[3520,"Each meeting has a **CRM Updates** tab of its own. It lists what was written after the call, such as **Account Updated** or **Contact Created**, and holds a stage move as a **Pending Update** until you press **Update Deal**."],[800,"Each meeting's **Coaching** tab shows the call's grade, a score out of 5 for each skill and a radar of your qualification criteria. A deal's **Coaching** tab grades how the rep ran that whole deal, with **Strengths** and **Focus Areas**."],[5101,"Each meeting's **CRM Updates** tab, in **Activities › Meetings**, lists what was written after the call. Completed cards such as **Account Updated** and **Contact Created** link to the record. A stage move waits as **Pending Update** until you press **Update Deal**."],[4913,"Each meeting's record in **Activities › Meetings** holds the results in seven tabs: **Overview**, **Action Items**, **Meeting insights**, **Recording**, **Coaching**, **Attendees** and **CRM Updates**. **Meeting insights** files what was said under each criterion of your framework, with timestamps into the call. It also says plainly when a criterion wasn't discussed, which is where the gaps show."],[4547,"Each model is further tuned to your business, because the pains a developer tools vendor hears differ from those a RevOps platform hears. Tuning runs on a short schedule:"],[1249,"Each Morning Brief meeting card shows a type tag, such as **Expansion** or **New Business**, the time and a short note. An availability line compares the meeting with your own calendar. **Add me to this call** and **Leave a note** let you join or brief the rep, and **Review Deal** opens the deal."],[2226,"Each new clip is posted to the Slack channel set for its moment, with a direct link to the clip. Each run's record carries **View Clip Library** and **View Slack Alert**, so you can jump to the clip or the message it sent. See Oliv AI integrations for the chat tools you can connect."],[1245,"Each open report has a **Rate this report** button and a date picker. The previous and next arrows step between editions of the same report. Olivia's daily brief also carries a Deal Driver section, such as a check-in draft for a quiet deal, with a **Review draft from Deal Driver** button."],[2919,"Each page in this section covers one part of working with captured conversations."],[1908,"Each piece of busywork is small: prep a meeting, follow up a call, update a field, brief a colleague on a handoff. Added up, it slows the whole team. A quiet deal often gets noticed only when a rep escalates it."],[4254,"Each plan carries everything in the plan below it, then adds one layer:"],[1767,"Each proposal opens in **Review changes** as a line-by-line diff of every file it touches, with its knock-on effects listed below. It waits as **Pending Review** until someone presses **Approve & merge**. That review step is covered in How the Oliver agent compares, below."],[4441,"Each proposed update includes its source, the exact moment in the conversation that triggered it. The **CRM Updates** tab shows the field, its current value and the suggested value."],[1317,"Each rep gets their own report on their own schedule, such as Every Thursday or Every Friday. It shows the rep's pipeline total, a Pipeline Summary and every deal by status."],[832,"Each rep's **Monthly Review** is listed under Coach in **Reports › My Reports**, scheduled every 30 days. The same review sits in **Apps › Enable › People**, under the rep's **Coach** section, with a list of past months."],[5613,"Each report opens in **Reports › My Reports** with a date picker to page through past editions and **Rate this report**. The same structure works for BDR and AE teams. Cadence and field configurations differ, but the briefs, alerts and rep reports work the same way."],[5413,"Each row shows the meeting's **Next Step** and **AI Summary**, and a **Meeting with** dropdown that classes it as Prospect, Customer, Candidate or Colleague. Click a row to open the meeting. Its **Overview** tab holds:"],[2190,"Each row's **Access Type** dropdown sets a library to **Public**, with a globe icon, or **Private**, with a lock. Use **+ New Library** to start one, and **Search**, **Group**, **Fields**, **Sort** and **Filter** to find one."],[375,"Each row's **Type** column says **Auto-triggered** or **Manually run**, so it's clear whether a person started the run. How other platforms record what their agents did is covered in How agent run history compares, below."],[3845,"Each run record keeps the Slack side in reach. The **Run History** drawer for a run shows the clip with its transcript, plus **View Clip Library** and **View Slack Alert** buttons."],[2372,"Each section holds evidence cards with timestamps. Where nothing was said, the card states it rather than guessing. The criteria follow the methodology active in **Settings › Qualification Framework**, so a team on another framework sees its own criteria."],[1512,"Each specialist agent owns one job. It does that job in the background and delivers the result where you already work, such as Slack, email or the Oliv AI app."],[4423,"Each step says what it did, such as the filters it built from your question. The signals step names the sources it read: meetings, CRM notes, emails and account news. You can check that logic before you act on the answer."],[4381,"Each suggested field change waits on the deal until someone accepts or rejects it, with the current CRM value shown beside it for comparison."],[5025,"Each suggested update shows the field, the current value, the proposed value and the moment in the conversation behind it. On a deal's **CRM Updates** tab, you **Accept** or **Reject** each AI suggestion. A meeting's **CRM Updates** tab lists what was written after the call and holds a stage move as a **Pending Update** until you click **Update Deal**. Switch to auto mode once you trust it."],[5139,"Each suggestion on the deal's **CRM Updates** tab can be accepted or rejected. How other platforms keep CRM fields current is covered in How keeping the CRM updated compares, below."],[1020,"Each suggestion shows the current value next to the suggested one, so you can reject it before it's written. **Updates History** keeps the record of every change."],[5177,"Each suggestion shows the field's current value beside the suggested one, so you can reject it before it's written. **Updates History** keeps the record of what changed."],[5108,"Each suggestion sits above the value it would replace, so reviewing takes a glance. Nothing in the CRM changes until you press Accept."],[552,"Each system's tools appear as cards with a one-line description. Gmail's nine run from reading and drafting to sending and deleting, which is why writes deserve a run mode check."],[2369,"Each task links to the moment in the recording where it was agreed. Tick a task off, change the **Pending** status filter, or press **Add task** to add one by hand."],[668,"Each trigger is written out on the tab. Every card shows the source system's icon, the event in one line and a sentence on when the agent fires. Runs it starts appear in the run history as **Auto-triggered**. How other platforms start agents on their own is covered in How agent triggers compare, below."],[5031,"Each workflow feeds the next one. The brief draws on what earlier calls captured. The call produces the follow-up and the field updates. Each 1:1 report reads the deal fields CRM Manager keeps current, so the review is only as good as that upkeep."],[4595,"Edit the deal's fields"],[2744,"Email and LinkedIn outreach"],[4264,"Email capture and optional Slack capture"],[3420,"Email capture is listed in the Converse app. The plans and seat roles guide explains how apps map to roles, and Oliv AI pricing has the current plans."],[3392,"Email features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[2883,"Email, LinkedIn and WhatsApp, each marked with a badge on the conversation. You can filter the Inbox by any one channel."],[4228,"Enable"],[4833,"Enable and Engage are add-ons, priced separately. Agent actions are billed separately from app subscriptions, through credits, on every plan. An agent action is a task an agent completes, such as researching an account or updating a CRM record. Current prices are on Oliv AI's pricing page."],[4299,"Enable evaluates customer conversations against coaching scorecards to identify where a rep needs help. It's an add-on, priced separately from the plans. In the app, its **Library** tab holds clip libraries, each **Public** or **Private**, and its **People** tab shows each rep's pacing for managers."],[3682,"Enable the **Advanced notes** functionality, which Oliv AI's guide points to as Salesforce's enhanced notes."],[2931,"Enable's People tab gives a manager the team's pacing at a glance. Each rep card opens that rep's report, which is where coaching conversations start."],[63,"Enablement"],[195,"Enablement"],[326,"Enablement"],[479,"Enablement"],[619,"Enablement"],[2023,"Enablement"],[2157,"Enablement"],[3112,"Enablement"],[3784,"Enablement"],[4976,"Enablement"],[1711,"Enablement leads"],[3857,"Enablement leads point Content Curator at a team channel, so new clips reach reps as they're found. Read more on Content Curator."],[766,"Enablement managers"],[4999,"Enablement managers use Oliv AI to ramp reps and keep training current. The Coach page shows how call scores turn into one goal per rep each month. The clip library collects the moments you describe, such as pricing objections, from real calls. Agent knowledge files hold the background reading an agent works against, such as a buying-committee profile or a solution deck."],[1801,"Enablement sees the effect through coaching. Coach coaches every rep against the methodology Oliver keeps current, so the standard reps are trained on matches the one agents enforce. The guide to sales methodology automation covers scoring calls against a framework."],[845,"Enablement sees which skills are actually winning deals and which training isn't sticking. Training can then be built from evidence, not assumptions. Read how coaching can cut new-hire ramp time and how sales enablement software differs."],[4229,"Engage"],[2726,"Engage app"],[2791,"Engage is an add-on, not a plan. You add it to Converse, Sell or Grow for the team members who connect with prospects and customers. Each Engage seat includes one connected primary mailbox and LinkedIn automation. For current prices, see Oliv AI pricing."],[2792,"Engage is for outbound teams that need to work the right accounts each day, with a reason to reach out. It gives SDRs, BDRs and their managers one workspace for ranking, outreach and calls."],[2880,"Engage is Oliv AI's sales engagement app. It brings replies into one Inbox, runs plays and flows, ranks accounts with a reason for each rank, and adds a power dialer."],[2776,"Engage is Oliv AI's sales engagement app. It gathers prospect replies from email, LinkedIn and WhatsApp in one Inbox, runs plays that enrol contacts on a signal or around the clock, and adds a power dialer with a call plan for every contact. Every account in a play carries its ICP fit and the signal behind it, so reps know who to work and why."],[2784,"Engage is where your reps prioritize, sequence, multi-thread, call and follow up, with the full account context attached. The product page puts its job plainly: it turns the context your team already creates into a ranked, executable workflow."],[2929,"Engage opens on its Inbox, where replies from every outreach channel arrive in one list. The tab bar shows the rest of the outreach workspace, from the dialer to experiments."],[2785,"Engage opens on the Inbox. Its six tabs split outbound work into replies, dialing, plays, flows, signals and experiments, and the left panel filters replies by disposition and channel."],[2811,"Engage ranks the accounts in each play by what matters now. A play's **Companies** tab lists every account with its **ICP Fit** grade and score, its **Engagement** (High, Medium or Low) and its **Point of View**: **Validated**, **Contextual**, **Hypotheses** or **Generic**."],[2856,"Engage reads the same account context as Oliv AI's CRM Manager agent and Oliv AI's Forecaster agent. Outreach and the deals it creates sit on one record. Keeping the CRM updated covers how activity reaches your CRM."],[4300,"Engage runs email and LinkedIn outreach from Oliv AI. Add it to Converse, Sell or Grow for team members who connect with prospects and customers. It includes one connected primary mailbox and LinkedIn automation. In the app, Engage has **Inbox**, **Dialer**, **Plays**, **Flows**, **Signals** and **Experiments** tabs. You can add more on top:"],[2731,"Engage the add-on"],[3054,"Engage turns buying signals into outreach: each play says what triggers it, how it reaches out and how many contacts are in it."],[2905,"Engage, Forecast and Enable"],[4651,"Even the match between a conversation and its record holds up on messy accounts. When one account carries several open opportunities, Oliv AI still files the conversation history against the right deal. That matching is one of the points covered in How Oliv AI compares as a CRM layer, below."],[3528,"Every