 or **Custom** badge, which tells you where that agent came from. A chat with Oliv AI's Oliver agent sits on the right of the marketplace, so you can ask about agents without leaving the screen. The panel has its own new chat and history buttons, a suggested question to start from and the **Ask before acting** setting under the message box."],[3850,"Some catalog agents start from a Slack message. Oliv AI's Product Release Messenger agent fires on a **Release announcement in #releases Slack channel**. It then uses **Monitor Slack channel**, **Read Slack message** and **Draft email** to turn release notes into customer updates for review."],[4954,"Some do. CRM Manager applies some updates, listed under **AI Updates** on the deal, and holds the rest under **AI Suggestions** for you to accept or reject. RevOps can switch to auto mode once accuracy thresholds are met."],[4450,"Some do. Forecaster learns from the signals you accept, edit or reject. Portfolio Manager learns from the flags you dismiss."],[827,"Some scorecards are written for a role, such as the solution engineer on a POC or the SDR on an event follow-up call. Every scorecard draws on a library of more than 100 criteria in six categories: Discovery & Qualification, Solution & Value, Stakeholder Alignment, Commercial & Negotiation, Risk & Competitive, and Foundational Skills. Managers add, remove or weight criteria to match their sales methodology, such as a SPICED scorecard."],[979,"Some teams prefer one review window a week. Reps get their pending CRM suggestions on Friday morning, and an auto-acceptance confirmation on Sunday night. If a rep doesn't complete updates within a set window, deals can be deferred automatically or flagged as closed-lost, depending on how your org configures it."],[5113,"Some teams run a weekly review window instead. Reps get their pending suggestions on Friday morning, and on Sunday night they get a confirmation of what was auto-accepted."],[5438,"Sometimes a colleague needs one part of the call, not all of it. Open the meeting's **Recording** tab, find the moment in **Chapters** or **Transcripts**, then use the buttons under the player:"],[4351,"Speaker attribution"],[2948,"Specialist agents"],[4744,"Specialist agents"],[1786,"Specialist agents carry a separate control on each of their tools, covered in agent tools and run modes."],[1105,"Stage values are the first mapping to confirm. Import them from the CRM here, then check that each stage rolls into the forecast category your reports expect."],[5497,"Stage, amount, close date, qualification fields and next steps, based on what was said on the call. A stage move waits for you to click Update Deal, and deal suggestions wait for Accept or Reject."],[3686,"Standard fields are mapped as soon as the connection is made. Oliv AI's team configures your custom fields during onboarding as a service, so there's no mapping task for your RevOps team."],[1173,"Standard fields are pre-mapped when you connect your CRM: close date, deal amount, stage, next steps and last activity date. They fill from day one."],[3261,"Start here"],[5259,"Start with the gaps. They're the questions worth asking while there's still time to act on the answers, which is the point of sales meeting preparation."],[5000,"Start with the section for your role above. If you own deals, begin with the account executive use case. If you manage people, begin with the pipeline review. If you run the systems, begin with Oliver and CRM upkeep. Each page links on to the agents and workflows it depends on."],[2518,"Stay on **My meetings**, or switch to **Team meetings** to see your team's calls too."],[3191,"Step 1 of a new cadence: name it, pick how often it repeats, and set separate days for reps and managers to submit."],[3086,"Step 1: Choose who runs the setup"],[5200,"Step 1: Connect your calendar, recorder and CRM"],[5039,"Step 1: Connect your CRM"],[5356,"Step 1: Get the call recorded"],[1041,"Step 1: List the fields you want kept current"],[5514,"Step 1: Set up Deal Driver"],[2522,"Step 1: the Activities menu holds Meetings and Calls, so this is where you start whenever you need to get back to a past customer conversation."],[1042,"Step 2: Connect your CRM"],[242,"Step 2: each row in Knowledge in use is one file the agent works against. Press View on any row to open it and check its content."],[5040,"Step 2: Let activity start the work"],[5201,"Step 2: Let the brief arrive before the call"],[3087,"Step 2: Line up admin access"],[5357,"Step 2: Read the meeting summary"],[1783,"Step 2: set how freely Oliv AI's Oliver agent may act in this conversation before you ask for a process change."],[5515,"Step 2: Start the day with the Morning Brief"],[1922,"Step 2: the picker lists both super agents with their own one-line descriptions. Choose Olivia for deals, meetings and next steps, and Oliv AI's Oliver agent for process questions."],[3088,"Step 3: Connect the stack in week one"],[1043,"Step 3: Create a HubSpot property for Oliv data"],[5516,"Step 3: Open each rep's One-on-One Prep"],[5202,"Step 3: Read the brief in about a minute"],[5041,"Step 3: Review proposed updates"],[5359,"Step 3: Review the follow-up draft"],[5360,"Step 4: Approve the CRM updates"],[5203,"Step 4: Ask Olivia to get you ready"],[3089,"Step 4: Build the process handbook"],[1044,"Step 4: Hand your field list to Oliv AI's team"],[1784,"Step 4: Oliv AI's Oliver agent answers a why question with a snapshot, then each cause and its impact. The figures are sample values."],[5042,"Step 4: Switch to auto mode when you're ready"],[540,"Step 4: the dropdown on each tool card lists the three run modes in the same fixed order, each with the icon it keeps on the button."],[688,"Step 4: the frequency comes first. The day and time dropdowns beside it follow whichever of the four you choose."],[5517,"Step 4: Work deal by deal"],[2524,"Step 5: a row opens the meeting's drawer on its Overview tab, so the takeaways and deal context are one click 