end. Read it, adjust anything that needs changing, and send it yourself. The pre-meeting brief for any active deal or customer works the same way: it informs you, and you decide what happens next."],[1669,"The follow-up is drafted within minutes of the call ending, once the recording is processed."],[4276,"The Forecast app page shows these views, and sales methodology tracking covers the frameworks."],[4816,"The Forecast app rolls each team up by period and snapshot, which is where a manager reads attainment, coverage and the commit number in one view."],[3184,"The Forecaster agent works from four settings. Set them in this order:"],[4216,"The four role-based Oliv AI plans, what each one adds, the add-ons that sit on top, and how to decide which person on your team needs which seat role."],[4219,"The four seat roles"],[1610,"The full tour of every tab is in meeting details."],[3342,"The Gmail integration is for deals that move as much by email as by meeting. It puts what the buyer wrote next to what the buyer said, on the same deal. People and agents then work from one record."],[3335,"The Gmail integration links your Google mailbox and calendar to Oliv AI. Gmail appears as one of two calendar integrations, next to Outlook, and as one of two email sources. Email threads are captured the same way as video calls and phone lines, so a deal's record holds both."],[871,"The goal is grounded in their own call data and deal outcomes, so the evidence is there to discuss. The aim is a data-led conversation, not a manager's opinion."],[1740,"The handbook is a set of structured, interlinked documents. Update the ICP, and the qualifying criteria across agents update with it."],[1748,"The handbook lives in **Playbook**, pinned at the bottom of the sidebar. A file tree groups markdown files into folders such as **Market**, **Prospecting** and **Sales**, with **Search playbook** above them. Each file opens on the **Edit** tab with a rich-text toolbar. A status row shows **Synced**