d to it, on one screen: files in use at the top, the upload area and import buttons below."],[2186,"The Library tab is the home of every clip library: each one has a name, a description of the moments it collects and an access type you can change from the row."],[4125,"The link to remove it in the meeting preparation summary, by email or in Slack."],[4126,"The link to remove it in the Zoom chat."],[3980,"The link to remove it in your meeting preparation summary, by email or in Slack."],[2496,"The list belongs to Converse, Oliv AI's conversation capture app. Online meetings are recorded one of two ways: botlessly through the meeting platform when your company hosts, or by a visible note taker when someone else does."],[241,"The list grows with the agent's job. A customer-facing agent can carry a playbook, response-time standards, FAQs and a file of approved attachments."],[353,"The list's columns depend on the agent. Every table carries **Time**, **Type** and **Status**. Some add more:"],[835,"The manager chooses the month's goal from three, each with its evidence, or keeps last month's goal running, so the rep only ever works on one."],[804,"The manager picks the goal that fits and sets it. Coach then breaks the goal into weekly sub-goals. At the end of each week the rep gets a progress report: progress on the goal, wins from last week, and one focus for next week."],[4519,"The mapping shows up wherever a record lists the people and activity tied to it. An account's **Contacts** tab groups people into **Buying Committee** and **Other Contacts**, each with a sentiment face. Select a person to see role tags such as **Economic Buyer**, plus their **Pain and Needs** and **Objections**, drawn from calls and emails. A contact's **Associated Objects** tab works the other way round: it lists every deal and company the person is tied to, with their role on each deal, such as **Champion** or **Technical Evaluator**."],[13,"The marketplace is where every agent starts. Cards show what each agent does and whether you view it or clone it, with Oliv AI's Oliver agent on hand for questions."],[1520,"The marketplace is where you find a specialist agent by team. Oliv AI's Oliver agent stays beside it, so you can ask a process question while you browse."],[3276,"The marketplace lists the specialist agents by team. Each card opens an agent page built from the parts described below."],[36,"The marketplace on oliv.ai offers pre-built agents designed for specific challenges, and invites you to request a custom agent. Oliv AI's GTM engineering team stays with you after launch. It reviews agent output, tunes the playbook and adds custom agents as your territory, comp or ICP shifts, as the RevOps page describes. A custom agent has the same parts as every other, so the pages in this section apply to it. The build vs buy guide covers when a custom agent makes sense."],[3353,"The matching holds when one account has several opportunities, as Where your emails land sets out above. How that lines up with other tools is covered in How the Gmail integration compares, below."],[4172,"The meeting bot asks for user_zak:read to join calls. The **Oliv.ai** app asks for meeting:read, user:read, meeting_token:read:local_recording and zoomapp:inmeeting. Each one is explained in the permissions table."],[5021,"The meeting summary is ready as soon as the call ends. Oliv AI's Meeting Assistant agent then drafts the follow-up email from the transcript, with the recap, commitments, owners and next steps already written. It also proposes CRM updates and flags qualification gaps. In **Activities › Meetings**, each meeting opens in a drawer with tabs for the overview, action items, meeting insights, the recording, coaching, attendees and CRM updates. The follow-up guide walks through reviewing each one, and the meeting details page shows the recorded call itself."],[5410,"The meeting summary is sent immediately after the meeting ends, to Slack and to your email by default. It