commendations."],[1859,"Things you can hand her"],[3821,"Think of a customer success team of six that runs its day from one shared Slack channel. Each CSM looks after around thirty accounts. When a customer hints at growth on a call, the team wants the account executive to hear about it the same day."],[1265,"Think of a regional sales leader with eight account executives and about forty open opportunities. Every Monday she walks the VP of Sales through the region's pipeline. On Friday she starts working out which of those forty deals are really moving."],[5135,"Think of a RevOps lead three days before the monthly board deck is due. The pipeline slide pulls straight from the CRM. She needs to trust every close date and stage in it, and she knows some haven't moved in weeks."],[233,"Think of an enablement manager who rebuilt the team's battlecards last month. She also keeps a set of one-page product sheets with no pricing in them. Reps were trained on both. Now an agent drafts answers for those same reps, and she wants it to say what they were taught."],[5334,"Thirty minutes before the meeting. You don't need to request it; it's sent automatically for meetings linked to an active opportunity."],[2967,"This catalog lists what Oliv AI does, grouped the way the product is organized. Each row says what the capability does and links the docs page that covers it, where one exists. Oliv AI's agents do the work, and every capability below feeds them or shows you what they did."],[5102,"This is Step 2 at work: one meeting refreshed the account, updated a scorecard and created two contacts. Only the stage move is left for a person to confirm."],[977,"This is the review step in Ask First. Every suggestion sits beside the value it would replace, and nothing changes until a rep presses Accept."],[3956,"This is the summary a Webex call produces: the key takeaways and AI summary, each point linked to its moment in the recording, plus the deal it belongs to."],[2678,"This is what a r